hadiths[600]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1","Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Uthman ibn al-Mughira informed us, saying: I heard Ali ibn Rabi'a al-Asadi narrating from Asma - or Abu Asma - al-Fazari, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah Almighty benefited me with whatever He willed that I be benefited. Ali said: And Abu Bakr narrated to me - and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, may Allah be pleased with him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no servant who commits a sin, then performs ablution and prays two rak'as, then seeks Allah's forgiveness, except that He forgives him. Then he recited this verse: {And those who, when they commit an immorality or wrong themselves, remember Allah and seek forgiveness for their sins} to the end of the verse, and the other verse: {And whoever does evil or wrongs himself} to the end of the verse."
"2","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughira, from Ali ibn Rabi'a, from Asma ibn al-Hakam al-Fazari, who said: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: Whenever I heard a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Allah benefited me with whatever He willed that I be benefited, and when anyone else narrated to me I made him swear that he heard it from him, then I believed him. And Abu Bakr narrated to me - and Abu Bakr spoke the truth, may Allah be pleased with him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said... then he mentioned similar to the hadith of Shu'ba."
"3","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, who said: Ubayd ibn al-Sabbaq informed me that Zayd ibn Thabit, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him, saying: Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, sent for me after the killing of the people of Yamama, and Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was with him. He said: This man came to me and informed me that the killing has intensified among the reciters of the Quran in this place - meaning the day of Yamama - and I fear that the killing will intensify among the reciters of the Quran in other places and the Quran will be lost, and I have decided that you collect it. I said to him - meaning to Umar - How can we do something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not do? Umar said to me: By Allah, it is good. Umar kept urging me until Allah opened my chest to that to which He had opened his chest, and I agreed with him. And you are an intelligent man, you used to write the revelation for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so we do not suspect you, therefore collect it."
"4","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Tawba al-Anbari, who said: I heard Abu al-Sawwar al-Anbari narrating from Abu Barza, who said: I was with Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was threatening a man and was harsh with him, so I said: Shall I strike his neck? Abu Bakr said: It is not for anyone after the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"5","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Khumayr informed me, saying: I heard Sulaym ibn Amir narrating from Awsat al-Bajali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, delivering a sermon. He mentioned the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and wept, then said - meaning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Hold fast to truthfulness, for it leads to righteousness, and both are in Paradise. And beware of lying, for it leads to wickedness, and both are in the Fire. And ask Allah for certainty and well-being, for people have not been given anything after certainty better than well-being - or he said: pardon - And do not envy one another, do not hate one another, do not cut ties with one another, do not turn your backs on one another, and be servants of Allah as brothers."
"6","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yahya ibn Talha ibn Ubayd Allah, who said: Isa ibn Talha informed me, from the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, who said: Whenever Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, mentioned the day of Uhud he wept, then said: All of that was Talha's day. Then he began to narrate, saying: I was the first to return on the day of Uhud, and I saw a man fighting alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) defending him - I think he said: protecting him. He said: I said: Let it be Talha, since I had missed what I missed. I said to myself: Let him be a man of my people, which is dearer to me. Between me and the east was a man I did not recognize, and I was closer to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) than he was, yet he was walking swiftly in a way I could not match, and behold it was Abu Ubayda ibn al-Jarrah. We reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his front tooth had been broken, his face wounded, and two rings of the helmet had entered his cheeks. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Tend to your companion, meaning Talha, who was bleeding, but he did not heed his words. I went to remove that from his face, but Abu Ubayda said: I adjure you by my right, leave me. So I left him. He disliked taking them with his hand lest he hurt the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so he bit onto them with his mouth and extracted one of the rings, and his front tooth fell out with the ring. I went to do what he had done, but he said: I adjure you by my right, leave me. He did as he had done the first time, and his other front tooth fell out with the ring. Thus Abu Ubayda became among the most handsome of people despite missing teeth. We tended to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we came to Talha in one of those pits, and behold he had some seventy wounds - or fewer or more - between stabs, arrows and strikes, and his finger had been cut off, so we tended to him."
"7","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sadaqa ibn Musa and Hammam narrated to us, from Farqad, from Murra, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The first to knock at the gate of Paradise is a servant who fulfilled the rights of Allah and the rights of his masters."
"8","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sadaqa ibn Musa and Hammam narrated to us, from Farqad, from Murra, from Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Neither a deceitful person nor a treacherous one will enter Paradise."
"9","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn Ata, who said: I heard Amr ibn Asim al-Thaqafi, who said: I heard Abu Hurayra saying: Abu Bakr al-Siddiq, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, command me something to say in the morning and in the evening. He said: Say: O Allah, Knower of the unseen and the seen, Originator of the heavens and the earth, Lord and Sovereign of all things, I bear witness that there is no deity but You, I seek refuge in You from the evil of my soul and from the evil of Satan and his polytheism. Say it in the morning, in the evening, and when you lie down."
"10","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, who said: I heard Salim ibn Abd Allah narrating from his father, that Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, sought permission from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for an Umra, so he permitted him and said to him: O my brother, include us in your supplication - or - do not forget us in your supplication."
"11","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from Salim, from his father, that Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, what we do - is it a new matter or something already decided? He said: Something already decided. Act, O son of al-Khattab, for each is facilitated. Whoever is among the people of happiness will do the deeds of happiness, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will do the deeds of wretchedness."
"12","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, steward of the family of al-Zubayr, from Salim, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever enters one of these markets and says: There is no deity but Allah alone, without partner, to Him belongs dominion and to Him belongs praise, He gives life and causes death, and He is the Living who does not die, in His hand is good, and He is over all things Capable - Allah Almighty will write for him a million good deeds, erase from him a million evils, and build for him a palace in Paradise."
"13","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Salim, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who sees an afflicted person and says: Praise be to Allah who has kept me safe from what He afflicted you with and preferred me greatly over many of those He created - except that affliction will not befall him, whatever it may be."
"14","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Asim ibn Ubayd Allah, from a man, from Ibn Umar, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wiping over the leather socks."
"15","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Ibn Umar, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dead is punished by the wailing over him in his grave."
"16","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl, who said: I heard Abu al-Hakam al-Sulami saying: I asked Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, about nabidh, and he narrated from Umar that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade earthen jars, gourds and pitch-coated vessels."
"17","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'ba narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Dinar narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn Umar saying: Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, I become junub at night, what shall I do? He said: Wash your private part, perform ablution, then sleep."
"18","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sakhr ibn Juwayriya narrated to us, Nafi' narrated to us, from Ibn Umar, that Umar saw a silk striped suit of Utarid al-Tamimi being sold. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, buy this suit and wear it on Friday and for delegations when they come to you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Only one who has no share in the Hereafter wears this. Later the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought similar suits and sent one to Umar. Umar came to him and said: O Messenger of Allah, today you sent me a suit though you said about Utarid's suit what you said. He said: Sell it for your benefit or clothe your women with it."
"19","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Juwayriya ibn Asma narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came upon Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, while he was swearing by his father. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) called out to him: Allah Almighty forbids you to swear by your fathers; whoever swears, let him swear by Allah or keep silent."
"20","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama, Hisham and Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about a man who divorced his wife while menstruating. He said: Do you know Ibn Umar? He divorced his wife while menstruating, and Umar mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Let him take her back."
"21","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Matar al-Warraq, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda al-Aslami, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Ibn Umar, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrated to me that he was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when a man came wearing two white well-kept garments, handsome in appearance, and said: May I come near you, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Come near. He kept drawing near until his knee was at the knee of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then he said: May I ask you? He said: Ask. He said: Tell me about Islam. He said: Testifying that there is no deity but Allah and that I am the Messenger of Allah, establishing prayer, giving zakat, pilgrimage to the House and fasting Ramadan. He said: If I do that am I a Muslim? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. The man said to him: You spoke the truth. We were amazed at his saying to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): You spoke the truth, as if he knew better than him. Then he said: O Messenger of Allah, tell me about faith. He said: Faith is to believe in Allah, His angels, His books, His messengers, resurrection after death, Paradise and Hell, and to believe in decree, its good and its evil. He said: If I do that am I a believer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Yes. He said: You spoke the truth. Then he said: Tell me what excellence is. He said: To fear Allah as if you see Him, for if you do not see Him, He sees you. He said: You spoke the truth. Then he said: Tell me about the Hour. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The one asked about it knows no more than the questioner. They are five that none knows but Allah: {Indeed Allah has knowledge of the Hour and sends down rain} to the end of the verse. The man said: You spoke the truth."
"22","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali, who said: I sat with Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no man who dies and three bear witness for him to good except Paradise becomes due for him. I said: O Messenger of Allah, and two? He said: And two. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was not asked about one."
"23","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated to us, from Ubayd ibn Hunayn, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: We came with Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, until we reached Marr al-Zahran. Umar entered the thicket to relieve himself and I sat waiting for him until he came out. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, I have wanted to ask you about a hadith for a year but your awe prevented me. He said: Do not do that; when you know I have knowledge, ask me. He said: I said: I ask you about the story of the two women. He said: Yes, Hafsa and Aisha. In ignorance we did not count women nor include them in our affairs. When Allah Almighty brought Islam and Allah placed them where He placed them and gave them a right without their entering our affairs, one day while I was sitting attending to something my wife said such-and-such to me. I said: What have you to do with this? When did you enter our affairs? She said: O son of al-Khattab, no one can speak to you, yet your daughter speaks to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he remains angry. I said: Does she really do that? She said: Yes. So I went to Hafsa and said: O Hafsa, do you not fear Allah? You speak to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until he remains angry. Woe to you, do not be deluded by Aisha's beauty and the Messenger of Allah's love for her. Then I went to Umm Salama also and said the same to her. She said: You have entered into everything, O son of al-Khattab, even between the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his wives. I had an Ansari companion who attended the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when I was absent and I attended when he was absent; he informed me and I informed him. None was more feared by us to attack us than a Ghassanid king. When Allah calmed the matter for us, one day while I was sitting my companion came crying: Abu Hafs, Abu Hafs! I said: Woe to you, what is it? Has the Ghassanid come? He said: No, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) has divorced his wives. I said: May Hafsa's nose be in dust! I put on my shoes and came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); in every house there was weeping, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was in an upper room with a black slave at the door. I said: Seek permission for me. He sought permission and he admitted me. He was sleeping on a mat with a leather pillow stuffed with fiber under his head, and tanned skins hanging. I told him what I had said to Hafsa and Umm Salama. He had sworn to stay away from his wives for a month; when the twenty-ninth night came he descended to them."
"24","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abd Allah, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not extol me as the Christians extolled Jesus son of Mary; I am only a servant, so say: the servant of Allah and His Messenger."
"25","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud'an, from Yusuf ibn Mihran, who said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, addressed us upon the minbar of Basra, saying: O people, Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, stood among us and said: O people, stoning is a prescribed punishment of Allah, so do not be deceived away from it, for it is in the Book of Allah and the Sunna of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned, Abu Bakr stoned, and I stoned."
"26","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd Allah al-Awdi, from Humayd ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, who said: Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, narrated to us, saying: I was the first to come to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, when he was stabbed. He said: O Abu Abbas, remember three things from me, for I fear people will not reach me: I have not decided about kalala, I have not appointed a successor over the people, and every slave of mine is free. It was said to him: Appoint a successor. He said: Whichever I do, one better than me has done it; if I appoint, one better than me appointed, and if I leave people to their affair, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left them. I said: Glad tidings of Paradise, O Commander of the Faithful; you accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) long, then ruled justly and fulfilled the trust. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: As for your glad tidings of Paradise, by Allah besides whom there is no deity, if I had all between heaven and earth I would ransom myself with it from what lies ahead before I know the outcome. As for Muslim affairs, by Allah I wish I escape from it evenly, neither against me nor for me. As for companionship of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that is that."
"27","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from Salama ibn Wahram, from Ikrima, from Ibn Abbas, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, that he performed tawaf and wished not to walk briskly, then said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) walked briskly only to enrage the polytheists. Then he said: It is something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did and did not forbid, so he walked briskly."
"28","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Uthman al-Qurashi of Mecca narrated to us, saying: I saw Muhammad ibn Abbad ibn Ja'far kiss the Stone and prostrate upon it, then he said: I saw your uncle Ibn Abbas kiss it and prostrate upon it. Ibn Abbas said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab kiss it and prostrate upon it, then Umar said: Had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss it, I would not kiss it."
"29","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu al-Aliya al-Riyahi, from Ibn Abbas, who said: Trustworthy men testified to me, among them Umar, and the most pleasing to me among them was Umar, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade prayer after Asr until the sun sets, and prayer after dawn until the sun rises."
"30","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn Mikhraq, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, from Uqba ibn Amir, who said: I entered the mosque while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was preaching. Umar said to me: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said before you came: Whoever dies believing in Allah and the Last Day, it will be said to him: Enter Paradise through whichever of the eight gates of Paradise you wish."
"31","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from Jabir ibn Samura, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us at al-Jabiya, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us as I stand among you, and said: Honor my Companions, then those who follow them, then those who follow them. Then lying will spread until a man swears though not asked to swear, and testifies though not asked to testify. Whoever desires the middle of Paradise, let him hold to the community, for Satan is with the lone one and farther from two. Let no man be alone with a woman, for the third of them is Satan. Whoever is pleased by his good deed and grieved by his evil deed is a believer."
"32","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Yazid narrated to us, from Mu'awiya ibn Qurra al-Muzani, who said: I came to Medina in the time of dried yogurt and ghee, when Bedouins brought burqan cloths to sell. I saw a man with raised gaze looking at people; I thought him a stranger, so I approached and greeted him. He returned my greeting and said: Are you of this town? I said: Yes. I sat with him and asked: From whom are you? He said: From Hilal, my name is Kahmas - or he said: from Banu Salul, my name is Kahmas. Then he said: Shall I narrate to you a story I witnessed from Umar ibn al-Khattab? I said: Yes. He said: While we were sitting with him a woman came and sat before him, saying: O Commander of the Faithful, my husband's evil is much and his good is little. Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Who is your husband? She said: Abu Salama. He said: That man has companionship and is truthful. Then Umar said to a man sitting with him: Is it not so? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, we know him only as you said. Umar said to a man: Rise and call him. The woman stood when he sent for her husband and sat behind Umar. Soon both came and sat before Umar. Umar said: What do you say about this one sitting behind me? He said: Who is she, O Commander of the Faithful? He said: This is your wife. He said: And what does she say? He said: She claims your good is little and your evil much. He said: Evil is what she said, O Commander of the Faithful; she is among the best of her women, most clothed and most comfortable, but her stallion is weak. Umar said: What do you say? She said: He spoke the truth. Umar rose to her with the stick and struck her with it, then said: O enemy of herself, you ate his wealth and consumed his youth, then speak ill of him falsely. She said: O Commander of the Faithful, do not hasten; by Allah I shall never sit in this gathering again. Then he ordered three garments for her, saying: Take for what I did to you, and beware complaining about this elder. As if I see her rising with the clothes. Then he turned to her husband and said: Let not what you saw me do to her make you mistreat her; depart. The man said: I would never do so. Then Umar said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The best of my nation is the generation I am from, then the second, then the third. Then will arise a people whose oaths precede their testimony; they testify without being asked, with clamor in their markets. Kahmas said to me: Do you fear these are among them? Then Kahmas said to me: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and told him of my Islam, then was absent a year, then came and said: O Messenger of Allah, as if you do not recognize me? He said: Yes, indeed. I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have not broken fast since I parted from you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who commanded you to torment yourself? Fast one day of the month. I said: Give me more. He said: Fast two days, until he said: Fast three days of the month."
"33","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Abu Rafi', that when Umar was stabbed, Suhayb said: Alas my brother, alas my brother. Umar said to him: Hush, my brother, hush O Suhayb, have you not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The dead is punished in his grave by his family's weeping."
"34","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A'la, from Suwayd ibn Ghafala, who said: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab kissing the Stone and saying: I kiss you knowing you are a stone, but I saw Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) devoted to you."
"35","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Khumayr, who said: I heard Habib ibn Ubayd narrating from Jubayr ibn Nufayr al-Hadrami, from Ibn al-Simt, that he heard Umar saying: I prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at Dhu al-Hulayfa two rak'as."
"36","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Amr, from a man, from Umar, who said: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with a group of people. A man came and said: O Messenger of Allah, who is best in station with Allah on Resurrection after His prophets and chosen ones? He said: The warrior in Allah's path with his soul and wealth until Allah's call comes to him while upon his horse holding its reins. He said: Then who? He said: A man apart who worships his Lord well and spares people his evil. He said: O Messenger of Allah, who is worst in station with Allah on Resurrection? He said: The polytheist. He said: Then who? He said: An unjust ruler who deviates from truth though empowered. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) secluded the doors of the unseen and said: Ask me, and whatever you ask I shall inform you. Umar said: We are pleased with Allah as Lord, Islam as religion, and you as prophet; what has come to us suffices us. He said: Then he was relieved."
"37","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd and Zuhayr ibn Muhammad al-Tamimi both narrated to us, both from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Muhammad ibn Ibrahim al-Taymi, who said: I heard Alqama ibn Waqqas al-Laythi saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: O people, deeds are only by intentions, and each person has only what he intended. Whoever emigrated to Allah and His Messenger, his emigration is to Allah and His Messenger. Whoever emigrated for worldly gain or a woman to marry, his emigration is to what he emigrated for."
"38","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abd Allah ibn Burayda, from Sulayman ibn al-Rabi' al-Adawi, who said: We met Umar and said to him: Abd Allah ibn Amr narrated to us such-and-such. Umar said: Abd Allah ibn Amr knows best what he says - he said it thrice. Then prayer was announced collectively, people gathered, and Umar addressed them, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A group of my nation will remain upon truth until Allah Almighty's command comes."
"39","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Fulayh ibn Sulayman al-Khuza'i narrated to us, saying: I heard al-Zuhri saying: Urwa ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from al-Miswar ibn Makhrama al-Qurashi and Ibn Abd al-Qari, that they heard Umar ibn al-Khattab saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me a sura of the Quran which I memorized. While I was standing praying in the mosque, Hisham ibn Hakim was praying beside me and recited that sura differently from how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had taught me. I almost seized him in prayer, then restrained myself until he finished. I seized his garment and said: Who taught you this verse? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me. I said: You lie; he taught me differently. I dragged him out. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw me he said: O Umar, let him go. I released his garment and said: O Messenger of Allah, you taught me a sura yet he recites differently. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Recite, O Hisham. He recited and he said: Thus it was revealed. Then he said to me: Recite, O Umar. I recited and he said: Thus it was revealed. The Quran was revealed upon seven modes, so recite what is easy of it."
"40","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Thabit al-Bunani, from Anas, who said: We looked for the crescent; none claimed to see it but me. I said to Umar: O Commander of the Faithful, do you not see it? I kept showing it to him, and when he could not see it he said: I shall see it lying on my bed. Then he told us about Badr, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informed us the day before of the enemies' deaths: This is the death place of so-and-so tomorrow, Allah willing; this is the death place of so-and-so tomorrow, Allah willing. By Him who sent him with truth, they did not miss those marks and fell upon them. Then they were thrown into the well. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and said: O so-and-so son of so-and-so, have you found what your Lord promised true? I have found what my Lord promised me true. I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you speak to bodies without souls? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Him in whose hand is my soul, you hear no better than they, but they cannot answer me."
"41","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, Ali ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Anas ibn Malik, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: I agreed with my Lord Almighty in four matters. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you prayed behind the Maqam, then this verse was revealed: {And take the Maqam of Ibrahim as a place of prayer}. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you veiled your wives, for the righteous and the wicked enter upon you, then Allah Almighty revealed: {When you ask them for something, ask them from behind a veil}. And this verse was revealed: {We created man from an extract of clay} to the end; when it was revealed I said: Blessed be Allah, the best of creators, then was revealed: {Blessed be Allah, the best of creators}. I entered upon the Prophet's wives and said to them: Either you desist or Allah will replace you with wives better than you, then was revealed: {Perhaps his Lord, if he divorces you} to the end."
"42","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, was stabbed, Hafsa wailed over him. Umar said: Have you not heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The one wailed over is punished."
"43","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Dhibyan saying: I heard Ibn al-Zubayr, may Allah be pleased with him, addressing people, saying: Do not clothe your women in silk, for I heard Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wears silk in this world will not wear it in the Hereafter."
"44","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Musa ibn Talha, from Ibn al-Hawtakiyya, who said: A rabbit was brought to Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: Were it not for fear I add or omit, I would narrate to you the Bedouin's story when he brought a rabbit to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned he saw blood on it, so he ordered them to eat it, and said to the Bedouin: Come near and eat. He said: I am fasting. He said: What fast do you keep? He said: From the beginning and end of the month. He said: If you fast, fast the white nights: the thirteenth, fourteenth and fifteenth. But send for Ammar. They sent for him and he came. He said: Do you witness that the Bedouin brought a rabbit to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I saw it bleeding? Ammar said: Yes."
"45","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Uqba al-Hadrami, from Ata ibn Dinar al-Hudhali, from Abu Yazid al-Khawlani, that he heard Fadala ibn Ubayd al-Ansari saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Martyrs are four: a believer of excellent faith who meets the enemy and is true to Allah, fighting until killed - he to whom people raise their eyes - and he raised his head until a cap upon his head, or upon Umar's head, fell - he is in the first rank. A believing man of excellent faith who, meeting the enemy, cowers as if acacia thorns pierce his skin; a stray arrow kills him - he is in the second rank. A believing man who mixed good and evil deeds, meets the enemy and is true to Allah until killed - he is in the third rank. And a man who wronged himself, meets the enemy and fights until killed - he is in the fourth rank."
"46","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Kharija ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Zayd ibn Aslam, from his father, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, that he gave a horse in Allah's path, then saw its owner had neglected it and wished to sell it. He asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about buying it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not buy it even for a dirham, for one who takes back his charity is like a dog returning to its vomit."
"47","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abd Allah, from Abd al-Rahman al-Musalli, from al-Ash'ath ibn Qays, who said: I stayed as Umar ibn al-Khattab's guest. He said: O Ash'ath, remember three things from me which I remembered from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Do not ask a man why he struck his wife, and do not sleep except upon witr - and I forgot the third."
"48","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan al-Thawri narrated to us, from Zubayd al-Yami, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Travel prayer is two rak'as, night prayer is two rak'as, and Friday prayer is two rak'as, complete not shortened, upon the tongue of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"49","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Asim ibn Amr al-Bajali, from one of the group who came to Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: O Commander of the Faithful, we ask you about three things: what is lawful for a man of his menstruating wife, bathing from major impurity, and reciting Quran in houses? Umar said: Glory be to Allah, are you sorcerers? You asked me what I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); none asked me after. He said: As for what is lawful of a menstruating wife, what is above the waist-wrapper; as for bathing, wash hands and private part, perform ablution, then pour water over head and body; as for reciting Quran, it is light - whoever wishes lights his house."
"50","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Sarjis saying: I saw Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, kiss the Stone then say: I kiss you knowing you are a stone; had I not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kiss you, I would not kiss you."
"51","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Haywa ibn Shurayh, from Bakr ibn Amr, from Abd Allah ibn Hubayra, from Abu Tamim al-Jayshani, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: If you truly relied upon Allah, He would provide for you as He provides birds: they leave hungry in the morning and return full in the evening."
"52","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, Abu Salama narrated to us, Abu Hurayra narrated to us, saying: While Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, was preaching on Friday, a man came. Umar said: Why do you delay for Friday? He said: O Commander of the Faithful, I only heard the call, performed ablution and came. He said: Ablution too? Have you not heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one of you goes to Friday, let him bathe?"
"53","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ma'dan ibn Abi Talha, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, preached on Friday, mentioning the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr, then said: I saw in a dream as if a rooster pecked me once or twice, and I see it only as my end approaching. People urge me to appoint a successor, yet Allah Almighty will not waste His religion nor His caliphate. By Him who sent His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), if my affair hastens, the caliphate is among these six men with whom the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) parted while pleased with them. Nothing after me concerns me more than kalala. Since I accompanied the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I never disputed with him as I disputed about kalala, nor was he harsh with me as he was about kalala, until he struck my chest with his hand and said: O Umar, the summer verse revealed at the end of Surat al-Nisa suffices you. O people, you eat from two trees I see only as foul: onion and garlic. I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he smelled them from a man, order him removed to al-Baqi'. Whoever must eat them, let him kill their smell by cooking."
"54","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Muhammad ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to us, Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Firas, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us saying: Whoever is wronged by his ruler, let him raise it to me and I shall retaliate for him. Amr ibn al-As stood and said: O Commander of the Faithful, if a man disciplines one of his subjects, will you retaliate against him? He said: How shall I not, when I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) retaliate against himself."
"55","Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Haytham ibn Rafi' narrated to us, Abu Yahya al-Makki narrated to us, from Umar ibn al-Khattab, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) preaching, saying: Whoever hoards his food against Muslims, Allah will afflict him with leprosy - or he said: with bankruptcy."
"56","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Adi ibn Adi, from his father, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: We used to recite among what we recited: Do not turn away from your fathers, for it is disbelief in you."
"57","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir saying: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab preaching, mentioning what was opened for people, and he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) writhing all day from hunger, not finding even poor dates to fill his belly."
"58","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash and Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from al-Subayy ibn Ma'bad, that he entered ihram for Hajj and Umra together, and mentioned it to Umar, who said: You have been guided to your Prophet's Sunna (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"59","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: al-Hakam informed me, from Abu Wa'il, that al-Subayy ibn Ma'bad was a Taghlibi Bedouin Christian who embraced Islam and asked: Which deed is best? He was told: Striving in Allah's path. He wished to strive, but was told: Have you performed Hajj? He said: No. He was told: Perform Hajj and Umra, then strive. He set out until at al-Hawait he entered ihram for both together. Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabi'a saw him and said: He is more astray than his camel - or no better guided than his she-camel. He went to Umar and told him what they said. He said: You have been guided to the Sunna of your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"60","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, hearing Murra, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: Three things - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) clarify them - are dearer to me than red camels: the caliphate, kalala and usury. I said to Murra: Who doubts kalala? It is what is besides child and parent. He said: They doubt about the father."
"61","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, saying: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari saying: I heard a hadith from a man which pleased me, and I wished to write it, so I said: Write it for me. He brought it written elegantly, saying: al-Abbas and Ali entered upon Umar, may Allah be pleased with them, disputing, while with Umar were Talha, al-Zubayr, Sa'd and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, may Allah be pleased with them. Umar said to them: I adjure you by Allah, do you not know, have you not heard that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the Prophet's wealth is charity except what he fed his family or clothed them; we are not inherited? They said: Yes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) spent from his wealth upon his family and gave the rest in charity."
"62","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Umar said: Rub the knees, for the knees have been made Sunna for you."
"63","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun saying: I witnessed Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, at Muzdalifa after dawn prayer. He stood and said: The polytheists would not depart until the sun rose, saying: Shine, Thabir. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) opposed them, so Umar departed before sunrise."
"64","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Abu al-Ajfa al-Sulami, who said: Umar ibn al-Khattab, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us saying: Do not inflate women's dowries, for had it been honor in this world and piety with Allah, Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would be most entitled to it. He married none of his daughters nor married any of his wives for more than twelve ounces. One of you inflates a woman's dowry until it becomes her ransom, saying: I suffered for you the rope's burden - or he said: the sweat of the waterskin."
"65","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sawwar ibn Maymun Abu al-Jarrah al-Abdi narrated to us, saying: A man of Umar's family narrated to me, from Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever visits my grave - or said: visits me - I shall be his intercessor - or witness. Whoever dies in one of the two Sanctuaries, Allah will raise him among the secure on Resurrection."
"66","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu Jamra informed me, saying: I heard Juwayriya ibn Qudama saying: I came to Medina and entered upon Umar when he was stabbed. He said: I enjoin you regarding the protected non-Muslims, for they are your Prophet's covenant (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"67","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, who said: I heard Tariq ibn Shihab narrating from Abu Musa, who said: Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: If we follow Allah's Book, Allah Almighty commanded completion; if we follow the Prophet's Sunna (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the Messenger of Allah did not exit ihram until the sacrificial animal reached its place."
"68","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Ibn Umar, that he divorced his wife while menstruating. Umar came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned it to him, so he counted it as one."
"69","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Budayl narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Ibn Umar, that Umar, may Allah be pleased with him, said: O Messenger of Allah, I had vowed to observe i'tikaf for a night in ignorance; what do you say? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Observe i'tikaf and fast."
"70","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Sayyar ibn al-Ma'rur, who said: I heard Umar ibn al-Khattab preaching, saying: O people, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) built this mosque with us, the Emigrants and Helpers. When crowding intensifies, let one of you prostrate upon his brother's back."
"71","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, Abu al-Malih al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, who said: I mentioned Talha to Umar, and he said: That is a man with pride since his hand was struck alongside the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"72","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id al-Ansari, from Abu Umama ibn Sahl ibn Hunayf, who said: We were with Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, in the house while besieged, entering through an entrance where we heard the speech of those in the courtyard. Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, entered then came out changed in color. It was said: O Commander of the Faithful, what is wrong? He said: They are threatening me with killing just now; I was not certain of them until today. We said: May Allah suffice you, O Commander of the Faithful. He said: For what would they kill me? I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The blood of a Muslim is not lawful except for one of three: a man who disbelieves after Islam, commits adultery after chastity, or kills a soul without right. By Allah, I never committed adultery in ignorance nor Islam, nor desired another religion since Allah guided me, nor killed a soul. For what do they wish to kill me?"
"73","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Alqama ibn Marthad al-Hadrami informed me, saying: I heard Sa'd ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of you are those who learn the Quran and teach it. Abu Abd al-Rahman said: That is what kept me in this seat."
"74","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Aban ibn Uthman, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One in ihram neither marries nor proposes."
"75","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, who said: I heard Humran ibn Aban narrating to Abu Burda, from Uthman ibn Affan, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever perfects ablution as Allah commanded, the prayers are expiations for what is between them."
"76","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham ibn Urwa, from his father, from Humran ibn Aban, that Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought ablution water for Asr prayer at al-Maqa'id. Uthman said: I have decided to narrate to you a hadith I did not think to narrate. Al-Hakam ibn Abi al-As said: O Commander of the Faithful, it is either good we follow or evil we avoid. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought ablution water at al-Maqa'id and said: Whoever performs ablution well, then prays completing its bowing and prostration, is forgiven what is between it and the next prayer so long as he does not commit a mortal sin - meaning: so long as he does not commit a major sin."
"77","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdala, from Musa ibn Talha, from Humran ibn Aban, from Uthman ibn Affan, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought ablution water at al-Maqa'id for Asr prayer, and said: When a Muslim performs ablution well, then prays the prayers - Hammad said: I think he said: in congregation - completing bowing and prostration, Allah forgives what is between them so long as he does not commit a mortal sin."
"78","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from a man, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man was easy in judging, claiming, selling and buying, so he entered Paradise."
"79","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Aban ibn Uthman, who said: I heard Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No servant says each morning or each evening: In Allah's name with whose name nothing harms on earth nor heaven, and He is the Hearing, Knowing - except nothing harms him. Aban had been struck by partial paralysis; a man entered and saw his condition, and Aban understood, saying: The hadith is as I narrated, but I did not say it that day so Allah's decree proceeds."
"80","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi al-Zinad narrated to us, from his father, from Amir ibn Sa'd, who said: I heard Uthman ibn Affan saying: By Allah, nothing prevents me from narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that I am not the most retentive of his hadith, but I bear witness I heard him saying: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"81","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abda ibn Abi Lubaba, from Abu Wa'il, from Uthman, that he performed ablution thrice each and said: Thus did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) perform ablution."
"82","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Awana narrated to us, from Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Amr ibn Jawan, from al-Ahnaf ibn Qays, who said: I heard Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, saying to Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas, Ali, al-Zubayr and Talha, may Allah be pleased with them: I adjure you by Allah, do you know the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever equips the army of hardship, Allah forgives him - so I equipped them until they lacked neither bridle nor rope? They said: O Allah, yes."
"83","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hurayth ibn al-Sa'ib narrated to us, saying: al-Hasan narrated to me, saying: Humran ibn Aban narrated to me that Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Everything besides a remnant of this food, sweet water and a sheltering house is surplus; the son of Adam has no merit therein."
"84","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahid ibn Zayd narrated to us, saying: Abd Allah ibn Rashid, freedman of Uthman, narrated to us, saying: My master Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty created one hundred and seventeen characters; whoever comes to Allah with one of them enters Paradise."
"85","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from Ayyub ibn Musa, from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Aban ibn Uthman, from Uthman, may Allah be pleased with him, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: When one in ihram complains of his eyes, aloes is dropped therein."
"86","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jarir ibn Hazim and Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Ya'qub, from Rabah, who said: My family married me to a Roman slave girl of theirs. She bore me a black boy like me, whom I named Abd Allah. Then I approached her again and she bore another black boy like me, whom I named Ubayd Allah. Then a Roman slave boy of ours called Yuhannas coveted her and had intercourse; she conceived and bore a boy like a gecko. I said: What is this? She said: By Allah, this is not from you; it is from Yuhannas. He said: She spoke the truth. They disputed before Uthman and both confessed. Uthman said: Will you accept my judging between you by the Prophet's judgment (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) judged the child belongs to the bed, and the adulterer gets the stone. He is your son; you inherit him and he inherits you. I said: Glory be to Allah. He said: It is so. I would put him to sleep between them - these two black and this white."
"87","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abu Ma'n, from Abu Salih, freedman of Uthman ibn Affan, who said: Uthman ibn Affan, may Allah be pleased with him, said in the mosque of al-Khayf: O people, a hadith I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) which I concealed from you sparing you; now I decide to disclose it as counsel: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: A day of one striving in Allah's path equals a thousand days otherwise, so let each of you look to himself."
"88","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Nafi', from Nubayh ibn Wahb, from Aban ibn Uthman ibn Affan, from his father, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: One in ihram neither marries nor proposes."
"89","Yunus narrated to us, Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Asim ibn Damra, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Witr is not obligatory, but a good Sunna from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Allah is One and loves the odd; so pray witr, O people of the Quran."
"90","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Sa'd ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Obedience is only in what is right."
"91","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Zibyan al-Janbi, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The pen is lifted from three: from the afflicted - or he said: the insane - until he recovers, from the child until he matures or understands, and from the sleeper until he awakes."
"92","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Mutarrif, from al-Sha'bi, from Abu Juhayfa, who said: We asked Ali: Do you have any revelation besides what is in Allah Almighty's Book? He said: No, by Him who splits the seed and creates the soul, I know only understanding Allah Almighty grants a man in His Book, or what is in this sheet. He said: I said: What is in it? He said: Blood money, freeing captives, and no Muslim is killed for a polytheist."
"93","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, who said: I heard al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymira narrating from Shurayh ibn Hani, who said: I asked Aisha about wiping over leather socks. She said: Ask Ali, for he traveled with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I asked him, and he said: Three days and nights for the traveler, and a day and night for the resident."
"94","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: al-Hakam informed us, saying: I heard Ibn Abi Layla saying: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us that Fatima, may Allah be pleased with her, complained of the mill's effect upon her hand. Captives were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); she went but did not find him, meeting Aisha, may Allah be pleased with her, informing her. When the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, Aisha told him of Fatima's coming. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came while we had taken our beds; we rose, but the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Stay in your places. He sat between us until I felt his feet's coolness upon my chest, and said: Shall I teach you better than what you asked? When you lie down, glorify Allah thirty-four times, declare His perfection thirty-three, and praise Him thirty-three; it is better for you than a servant."
"95","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Yahya ibn al-Jazzar, from Ali, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that on the day of the Confederates he was at an opening of the trench and said: They distracted us from the middle prayer until the sun set; may Allah fill their graves and houses with fire - or their graves and bellies with fire."
"96","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ali ibn Husayn, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, who said: I witnessed Uthman and Ali, may Allah be pleased with them both, between Mecca and Medina, while Uthman forbade mut'a or combining both. When Ali saw that, he entered ihram for both together, saying: Here I am for Umra and Hajj together. Uthman said: Do you see me forbidding people something while you do it? He said: I would not abandon the Prophet's Sunna (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for anyone's word."
"97","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from a Basran man - Basrans call him Abu al-Muwarri', Kufans call him Abu Muhammad, of Hudhayl - from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at a funeral and said: Which of you will go to Medina leaving no idol unbroken, no image undefaced, no grave unleveled? A man rose saying: O Messenger of Allah, I will. He went but feared Medina's people and returned. Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, went and returned saying: I did not come to you, O Messenger of Allah, until I broke every idol, leveled every grave, and defaced every image. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever returns to making any of these - speaking harshly about it - and said to Ali: Do not be a troublemaker, nor arrogant, nor a trader except a trader in good, for those are foremost in deeds."
"98","Abu Dawud narrated to us, from Abu Awana, from Jabir, from Abd Allah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade animals with cropped ear or horn for sacrifice."
"99","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Jurayy ibn Kulayb, hearing Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade sacrificing an animal with cropped ear or horn. Qatada said: I asked Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib about cropping, and he said: Half or more."
"100","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murra, hearing Abu al-Bakhtari saying: One who heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to me, saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, I said: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me while I am young in age with little knowledge of judgments. He struck his hand upon my chest and said: Allah Almighty will steady your tongue and guide your heart; no judgment between two has ever baffled me."
"101","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, hearing Abu al-Bakhtari narrating from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: I heard Ali saying: When I narrate to you a hadith from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), think of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as the most pleasant, most guided and most pious."
"102","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: Ali and Uthman, may Allah be pleased with them both, met at Usfan. Uthman forbade mut'a, so Ali said: What do you intend toward something the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did, forbidding it? Uthman said: Leave us alone from you. He said: I cannot leave you. When he saw that, he entered ihram for both together."
"103","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, hearing Abd Allah ibn Salima saying: I entered upon Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, with two men - one of us and one of Banu Asad, I think. He sent them off and said: You are two stout men, so strive for your religion. Then he entered the lavatory, came out, took a handful of water and wiped with it, then recited Quran. Seeing our disapproval, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would enter the privy, relieve himself, then come out, eat meat with us and recite Quran; nothing barred him from Quran except major impurity."
"104","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Shaddad saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) never mentioned both his parents for anyone except Sa'd, for he said to him on Uhud: Shoot, Sa'd, may my father and mother be ransom for you."
"105","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ibrahim ibn Abd Allah ibn Hunayn, from his father, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to recite Quran while bowing, to wear saffron-dyed clothes, and to wear a gold ring."
"106","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Mundhir al-Thawri narrating from Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was shy to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy because of Fatima, so I ordered a man who asked him. He said: Ablution is due for it."
"107","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Awn ibn Abi Juhayfa informed me, saying: I heard my father saying: I heard Ali saying: When I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), falling from the sky is dearer to me than saying about the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what he did not say. When I narrate my opinion, war is deceit."
"108","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Warqa narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash - Shu'ba said: from Ali, and Warqa said: from Rib'i, from a man, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him - that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No servant believes until he believes in four: testifying there is no deity but Allah and that I am Allah's Messenger sent with truth, believing in death, believing in resurrection, and believing in decree."
"109","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Mansur informed me, saying: I heard Rib'i ibn Hirash saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, preaching, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not lie about me, for whoever lies about me enters the Fire."
"110","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrating from Wahb ibn al-Ajda', from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not pray after Asr, unless you pray while the sun is high."
"111","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Sa'd ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent an expedition appointing a man over them, commanding obedience to him. He kindled a fire and ordered them to plunge into it. Some intended to do so, while others said: We fled from the Fire. They refused. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and it was mentioned to him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had they entered it, they would remain therein until Resurrection. There is no obedience to a human in disobedience to Allah Almighty; obedience is only in what is right."
"112","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ali ibn Mudrik, who said: I heard Abu Zur'a ibn Amr ibn Jarir narrating from Abd Allah ibn Nujayy, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Angels do not enter a house wherein is an image nor one in major impurity."
"113","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn Uyayna and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salama both narrated to us, both hearing al-Zuhri saying: al-Hasan and Abd Allah, sons of Muhammad ibn al-Hanafiyya, narrated to me from their father, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said to a man giving fatwa about mut'a: Look what you give fatwa about? I bear witness the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade temporary marriage and eating domestic donkey meat."
"114","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Za'ida narrated to us, from al-Suddi, from Sa'd ibn Ubayda, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, addressed us saying: O people, establish prescribed punishments upon your slaves, married or unmarried, for a slave girl of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed adultery, and he ordered me to flog her. I came to her and found her recently delivered; fearing she would die if flogged, I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informing him. He said: You did well."
"115","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama, Qays and Sallam all narrated to us, all from Simak ibn Harb, from Khalid ibn Ar'ara, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the House collapsed after Jurhum and Quraysh rebuilt it, they disputed who would place the Stone, agreeing the first to enter this door would place it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered from Banu Shayba's door. He ordered a cloth, placed the Stone in its middle, and ordered each tribe to hold a side and lift it; then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took and placed it."
"116","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama, Qays ibn al-Rabi' and Abu Awana - all - narrated to us, all from Simak ibn Harb, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir al-Kinani: Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, narrated to us, saying: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, people dug a pit for a lion. People crowded upon the pit; the lion fell in, then a man fell in, grasping another, and another grasping another, until four. The lion wounded them inside and they perished. People bore arms, nearly fighting. I came saying: Will you kill two hundred men for four? Come, I judge between you; if pleased it is judgment, else raise to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), most entitled to judge. He assigned the first a quarter blood money, the second a third, the third half, the fourth full, imposing them upon those present at the pit, the four tribes. Some were angry, some pleased. They came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrating the story. He said: I judge between you. One said: Ali already judged between us, informing him of Ali's judgment. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Judgment is as Ali judged - this is Hammad's wording - and Qays said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) upheld Ali's judgment."
"117","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Asim ibn Damra al-Saluli saying: I heard Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed witr in every part of night: its beginning, middle and end, ending his witr at dawn."
"118","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Haritha ibn Mudarrib saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: You saw us on Badr's night with all asleep except the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who prayed by a tree supplicating. None among us was mounted except al-Miqdad, may Allah be pleased with him."
"119","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Hani ibn Hani saying: I heard Ali saying: Ammar sought permission upon the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The good, perfumed one - admit him."
"120","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Hubayra narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would wake his family in the last ten nights."
"121","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Hubayra ibn Yarim saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: A silk suit was gifted to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who sent it to me. I wore it, and he said to me: I am not pleased for you with what I dislike for myself. He ordered me, so I cut it into headscarves among women."
"122","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Najiya ibn Ka'b saying: I witnessed Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: When my father died I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Your uncle has died. He said: Go and bury him. I said: He died a polytheist. He said: Go bury him and do nothing until you come to me. I did so, then came to him, and he ordered me to bathe."
"123","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: al-Fudayl Abu Mu'adh informed me, from Abu Hariz al-Sijistani, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, said: When I returned to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having buried him, he said to me words I would not exchange for the world."
"124","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Najiya ibn Ka'b, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) after burying Abu Talib, he supplicated for me with supplications."
"125","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Hisham al-Fazari, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Harith ibn Hisham, from Ali ibn Abi Talib, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would say in his witr: O Allah, I seek refuge in Your pleasure from Your anger, in Your pardon from Your punishment, and I seek refuge in You from You. I cannot count Your blessings nor praise of You; You are as You praised Yourself."
"126","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I have exempted you from charity on horses and slaves; bring a quarter of a tenth: from every forty dirhams, one dirham."
"127","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik, Za'ida and Sulayman ibn Mu'adh narrated to us, saying: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Hanash ibn al-Mu'tamir, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me to Yemen, I said: You send me young with little knowledge of judgments. He said: When two litigants come, do not judge for the first until you hear what the other says; when you hear the other you will know how to judge. Allah Almighty will steady your tongue and guide your heart. Ali said: I remained a judge thereafter."
"128","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray witr at the call to prayer, and pray two rak'as at the iqama."
"129","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Asim ibn Damra saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would pray Duha."
"130","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I heard Asim ibn Damra saying: I asked Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about the Prophet's prayer (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He mentioned four before Zuhr, two after Zuhr, and four before Asr."
"131","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Hani ibn Hani narrating from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: When al-Hasan ibn Ali was born I said: Name him Harb. I wished to be called Abu Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came and called for him, saying: What did you name him? We said: We named him Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather he is al-Hasan. When al-Husayn was born we named him Harb. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came saying: What did you name him? We said: Harb. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is al-Husayn."
"132","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Hani ibn Hani, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: Al-Hasan ibn Ali most resembled the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) from his face to his navel, and al-Husayn most resembled the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) below that."
"133","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu al-Khalil - Abu Dawud said: his name is Abd Allah ibn al-Khalil - saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: A man prayed beside me; I heard him seeking forgiveness for his parents though they died polytheists. I said: Do you seek forgiveness for your parents though they died polytheists? He said to me: Ibrahim sought forgiveness for his parents. I did not know what to answer. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioning it, whereupon Allah Almighty revealed: {Ibrahim's seeking forgiveness for his father} to the end."
"134","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ali ibn Rabi'a al-Asadi, who said: I witnessed Ali when a mount was brought for him to ride. Placing his foot in the stirrup, he said: In Allah's name. Settling upon its back, he said: Praise be to Allah, thrice, and said: Allah is Greatest, thrice. Then he said: Glory be to You, I wronged myself, so forgive me; none forgives sins but You. Then he laughed. I said: O Commander of the Faithful, why did you laugh? He said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as I did, then laugh. I said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you laugh? He said: Your Lord Almighty marvels at His servant when he says: Forgive my sins, knowing none forgives sins but He."
"135","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, from Hubayra and Ali's companions, from Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade - or forbade me - ji'a, a barley drink that intoxicates."
"136","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Amr ibn Murra informed me, saying: I heard Abd Allah ibn Salima saying: I heard Ali saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to me while I was ill, saying: O Allah, if my term has come, relieve me; if delayed, raise me; if trial, grant patience. He struck me with his foot saying: What did you say? I repeated to him. He said: O Allah, heal him - or said: O Allah, grant him well-being. Ali said: I never complained of my pain thereafter."
"137","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Za'ida narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I was a man emitting much madhiy, and the Prophet's daughter (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was with me. I ordered a man who asked him about madhiy. He said: When you see it, perform ablution and wash it."
"138","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Za'ida narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from Husayn ibn Qabisa al-Fazari, from Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about madhiy. He said: When you see madhiy, perform ablution and wash your private part; when you see spurting fluid, bathe."
"139","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Waki' and Sallam both narrated to us, both from Abd al-A'la ibn Amir, from Abu Jamila, from Ali, that a slave girl of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) committed adultery. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) ordered me to apply the punishment. I came to her and found her blood not yet dried. I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) informing him. He said: When her blood dries, flog her. Establish punishments upon those your right hands possess."
"140","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu Awn al-Thaqafi informed me, saying: I heard Abu Salih al-Hanafi saying: I heard Ibn al-Kawwa ask Ali about a foster brother's daughter. Ali said: I mentioned Hamza's daughter to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: She is my foster brother's daughter."
"141","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara informed me, saying: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabra saying: Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, prayed Zuhr in al-Rahba, then sat attending to people's needs until Asr came. Then a jug of water was brought; he poured a handful washing his face and hands, wiped his head and feet, then stood and drank the remaining water standing. Then he said: People dislike drinking while standing, yet I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) do as I did. And he said: This is the ablution of one who did not break his ablution."
"142","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Malik ibn Urfuta, from Abd Khayr al-Khaywani, that Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, was brought a chair and sat upon it. Then a jug of water was brought; he washed his hands thrice, rinsed his mouth thrice with sniffing, washed his face thrice with one hand, washed his forearms thrice, put his hand in the vessel then wiped his head, moving his hands forward over his head - I know not whether he moved them back - and washed his feet thrice. Then he said: Whoever wishes to see the Prophet's purification (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), this is the Prophet's purification."
"143","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu Awn al-Thaqafi informed me, saying: I heard Abu Salih al-Hanafi saying: I heard Ibn al-Kawwa ask Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, about a foster brother's daughter. Ali said: I mentioned Hamza's daughter to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: She is my foster brother's daughter."
"144","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysara informed me, saying: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabra saying: Ali prayed Zuhr in al-Rahba, then sat attending to people's needs until Asr came."
"145","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: Mas'ud ibn al-Hakam informed me, saying: I heard Ali, may Allah be pleased with him, saying: We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stand, so we stood; then we saw him sit, so we sat. Shu'ba said: I said to Muhammad: About the funeral, meaning? He said: Yes."
"146","Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from Mansur, from Sa'd ibn Ubaydah, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We went out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for a funeral until we reached Baqi al-Gharqad. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sat down and we sat around him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a stick and tapped the ground with it, then raised his head and said: There is no living soul but its place in Paradise and its place in Hell has been known - or written - and whether it is wretched or blessed. A man from the people said: O Messenger of Allah, should we then abandon deeds and rely upon our decree? Whoever of us is among the people of blessedness will act for it, and whoever of us is among the people of wretchedness will act for it. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Act, for each is facilitated. Whoever is among the people of blessedness will be facilitated to its deeds, and whoever is among the people of wretchedness will be facilitated to its deeds. Then he recited: {As for he who gives and fears Allah, and believes in the best reward, We will facilitate for him the easy path. But as for he who withholds and considers himself free of need, and denies the best reward, We will facilitate for him the difficult path.}"
"147","Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Aziz ibn Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to us, he said: My uncle al-Majishun Abd Allah ibn Abi Salamah narrated to me, from Abd al-Rahman al-A'raj, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Rafi', from Ali, he said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) began the prayer he would say takbir, then say: I have turned my face to the One who originated the heavens and the earth, inclining to truth, and I am not among the polytheists. Indeed my prayer and my sacrifice and my living and my dying are for Allah, Lord of the worlds. He has no partner, and with this I have been commanded, and I am the first of the Muslims. O Allah, You are the King, there is no god but You. You are my Lord and I am Your servant. I have wronged myself and I confess my sin, so forgive me all my sins, for none forgives sins but You. Guide me to the best of character, none guides to its best but You, and turn its evil away from me, none turns its evil away but You. Here I am at Your service, all good is in Your hands, and evil is not attributed to You. I am through You and to You. Blessed and exalted are You. I seek Your forgiveness and repent to You. And when he bowed he would say: O Allah, to You I have bowed, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My hearing and my sight, my bones, my marrow and my sinews have humbled themselves to You. And when he raised his head he would say: Allah hears the one who praises Him. O Allah, our Lord, to You belongs praise, filling the heavens and filling the earth, and filling what is between them, and filling whatever You will beyond that. And when he prostrated he would say: O Allah, to You I have prostrated, in You I have believed, and to You I have submitted. My face has prostrated to the One who created it and fashioned it and made its form excellent, and split open its hearing and sight. Blessed is Allah, the best of creators. And when he gave the salutation he would say: O Allah, forgive me what I have done before and what I do after, what I have done openly and what I have done secretly, and what You know better than I. You are the One who brings forward and You are the One who puts back. There is no god but You. Abu Bishr said: Abu Dawud said: This is in the night prayer."
"148","Abu Dawud said: Warqa' narrated to us, from Abd al-A'la, from Abu Jamilah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) underwent cupping, and he commanded me, so I paid the cupper his fee."
"149","Abu Dawud said: al-Ash'ath ibn Sa'id narrated to us, Abd Allah ibn Bishr narrated to us, from Abu Rashid al-Hubrani, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wound a turban around my head on the day of Ghadir Khumm, letting its end hang behind me, then said: Allah Almighty reinforced me on the days of Badr and Hunayn with angels wearing this turban. Then he said: The turban is a barrier between disbelief and faith. And he saw a man shooting with a Persian bow, so he said: Throw it away. Then he looked at an Arab bow and said: Hold to this and its like, and to spears of cane, for through these Allah will establish you in the lands and support you with victory."
"150","Abu Dawud said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, from Abu Wa'il, from Ibn Abi al-Hayyaj, from his father, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said to me: I employ you for what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) employed me for: effacing images and leveling graves."
"151","Abu Dawud said: Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Salim ibn Abi al-Ja'd, from Ali ibn Alqamah, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: It was said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Should we breed the donkey onto the horse? He said: Only those who do not know do that."
"152","Abu Dawud said: Sharik narrated to us, from Uthman ibn al-Mughirah, from Zayd ibn Wahb, he said: The leader of the Khawarij came to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and said to him: Fear Allah, for you shall die. He said: No, by the One who split the grain and created the soul, but I shall be killed by a blow from this that will dye this - and he pointed with his hand to his beard - a solemn covenant and a decreed decree. Ruined indeed is he who invents lies."
"153","Abu Dawud said: Abu Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Mughirah ibn Hadhf, from Ali, or Hudhayfah (may Allah be pleased with them both), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made the Muslims partners in their sacrificial animals: a cow suffices for seven."
"154","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Muslim al-A'war informed me, he said: I heard Habbah al-Urani narrating from Ali, that a man said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): A man loves a people but cannot perform deeds like theirs. He said: A person is with whom he loves."
"155","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, he said: I heard Hujayyah ibn Adi narrating from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to examine the eye and the ear closely."
"156","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, he said: I heard Abu Burdah saying: I heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a house, and he said: O Ali, ask Allah for guidance, and recall through guidance your guiding of the way, and ask Allah for uprightness, and recall through uprightness your straightening of the arrow."
"157","Abu Dawud said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from Abd Allah ibn Sakhbarah, he said: We were sitting with Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) waiting, when a funeral passed by us, so we stood for it. He said: What is this? We said: This is what you bring to us, O companions of Muhammad. Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrated to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the funeral of a Muslim man, or a Jew, or a Christian passes by you, stand for it, for we do not stand for it, but we stand for those with it among the angels. Ali said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did it only once, and they were People of the Book; he would imitate them in a matter, and when he was forbidden, he desisted."
"158","Abu Dawud said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, he said: The killer of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam sought permission to enter upon Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him). Ali said: By Allah, the killer of the son of Safiyyah shall surely enter Hell. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Every Prophet has a disciple, and my disciple is al-Zubayr."
"159","Abu Dawud said: Qays narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The middle prayer is the Asr prayer."
"160","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Hakim and Nu'aym ibn Hakim, both from Abu Maryam, he said: I heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Some people of my Ummah will recite the Qur'an and it will not pass beyond their collarbones; they will shoot out of Islam as the arrow shoots out of the prey. Their sign is a man with a deformed hand. Abu Maryam said: My brother informed me - and he had gone out with his freedman to the Haruriyyah at al-Nahrawan - he said: He did not come to them until they had killed his messenger. When he saw that, he rose against them and fought them. When he finished with them he said: Seek the deformed one. Messengers kept going back and forth but could not find him. Then a man came afterward and gave him glad tidings, saying: We found him in a low patch of ground beneath two men. So he cut off his hands and the lump, took it and set it up, and said: By Allah, I have neither lied nor been lied to. He said it repeatedly."
"161","Abu Dawud said: Sa'id ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, he said: Ubaydah al-Salmani said: I inform you only of what Ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me of: Among them is one with a small hand - or a deformed hand, or a hand with a lump - were it not that you would become overconfident, I would inform you of what Allah has promised to whoever kills them upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So I said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): Did you hear it from Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Yes, by the Lord of the Ka'bah. He said it three times."
"162","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Kulayb, I heard Abu Burdah, he heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade me to wear a ring on the middle finger and the one next to it."
"163","Abu Dawud said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Shimr ibn Atiyyah, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah al-Ju'fi, he said: Ali used to go out to the market and say: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. It was said to him: Your saying: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth? He said: Allah and His Messenger have spoken the truth. When I narrate to you from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), by Allah, for me to fall from the sky and the birds snatch me away is dearer to me than to say: I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what I did not hear. And when I narrate to you from myself, then war is deceit. I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will come in the last age a people young in age, foolish in minds, speaking from the speech of the best of creation, reciting the Qur'an and it will not pass beyond their throats. They will shoot out of the religion as the arrow shoots out of the prey. Whoever reaches them, let him kill them or fight them, for whoever kills them will have a reward in killing them on the Day of Resurrection."
"164","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Jamil ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Wadi' al-Suhaymi, he said: We were with Ali ibn Abi Talib at al-Nahrawan. He said: Seek the deformed one. So they sought him and did not find him. They came to him, and he said: Go back and seek him, for by Allah, I have neither lied nor been lied to, until he said that to me repeatedly. So they returned and said: We found him beneath the slain in the mud. It is as if I am looking at him now, an Abyssinian, with a breast like a woman's breast, upon it small hairs like the small hairs on the tail of the jerboa. Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) rejoiced at that."
"165","Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: No servant tastes the flavor of faith until he believes in all of the decree."
"166","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Uthman ibn Abd Allah ibn Hurmuz, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was neither short nor tall, large of head and beard, thick in the palms and feet, large of joints, his face tinged with redness, long of the line of hair on the chest, when he walked he leaned forward energetically, as if descending a slope. I never saw anyone like him before him nor after him."
"167","Abu Dawud said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Ibn Dhi Huddan, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: Allah Almighty named war upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as deceit."
"168","Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Aziz ibn al-Mukhtar narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Fayruz, from Hudayn Abu Sasan al-Raqashi, he said: I was present with Uthman ibn Affan (may Allah be pleased with him) when al-Walid ibn Uqbah was brought, having drunk wine, and Humran ibn Aban and another man testified against him. Uthman said to Ali: Carry out the hadd upon him. Ali ordered Abd Allah ibn Ja'far Dhi al-Janahayn to flog him. He began flogging him while Ali counted, until he flogged forty. Then he said to him: Stop. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) flogged forty, Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged forty, and Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) flogged eighty, and each is a Sunnah, and this is dearer to me."
"169","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, from a man of Anazah, from a man of Banu Asad, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came out to us when the caller pronounced the second call, and said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded the witr and appointed for it this hour. Call the adhan, O Ibn al-Nabbah - or: pronounce the iqamah, O Ibn al-Nabbah."
"170","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Zadham, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever leaves a hair untouched by water from janabah, Allah will do such and such with it of Hell. Therefore I treated my head - or he said: my hair - as an enemy, and he used to cut his hair short."
"171","Abu Dawud said: Abd al-Rahman ibn Thabit ibn Thawban narrated to us, from Abdah ibn Abi Lubabah, from Abu Wa'il, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed wudu three times three times."
"172","Abu Dawud said: Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, I had one hundred uqiyyahs and I gave ten uqiyyahs of it in charity. Another said: O Messenger of Allah, I had one hundred dinars and I gave ten dinars of it in charity. Another said: O Messenger of Allah, I had ten dinars and I gave one dinar of it in charity. He said: Each of you has done well, and you are equal in reward; each man of you gave a tenth of his wealth in charity."
"173","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Habbah al-Urani, he said: I heard Ali saying: I am the first who prayed with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"174","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that when he passed by the Black Stone and saw crowding upon it, he would face it and say takbir, and say: O Allah, in affirmation of Your Book and the Sunnah of Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"175","Abu Dawud said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) decreed debt before bequest, while you recite: {after any bequest he may have made or debt}. And that full brothers from the same mother inherit to the exclusion of half-brothers through the father."
"176","Abu Dawud said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah, he said: I witnessed Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) when he was asked about Hudhayfah. He said: He asked about the names of the hypocrites and was informed of them. He was asked about himself, and said: Myself I knew. When I asked, I was answered, and when I was silent, I was addressed first."
"177","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah, he said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb saying: I heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent me a striped silk garment - meaning of silk - so I wore it and went out in it. He saw anger on his face and said: I did not send it to you to wear it. He said: So I divided it among our womenfolk, or: my wives."
"178","Abu Dawud said: Isra'il narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Harith, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Ali, I love for you what I love for myself, and I dislike for you what I dislike for myself. Do not recite while bowing, nor while prostrating, and do not pray with your hair tied up, the resting place of Satan, and do not play with pebbles while in prayer, and do not wear a gold ring, and do not wear qassi garments, nor ride upon soft saddle cloths."
"179","Abu Dawud said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Umayr ibn Sa'id al-Nakha'i, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: There is no one upon whom I carried out a hadd and he died that I would pay blood money for him, except the hadd for wine, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not establish it as a Sunnah - or he said: except the hadd for wine, for we established it."
"180","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We have nothing but the Book of Allah, and this sheet from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Madinah is a sanctuary between Ayr and Thawr. Whoever introduces an innovation in it, or shelters an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept from him any obligatory or supererogatory deed. And whoever takes as allies a people without the permission of his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people; no obligatory or supererogatory deed will be accepted from him."
"181","Abu Dawud said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from al-Hajjaj, from al-Hakam, from Maymun ibn Abi Shabib, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave me two young servant boys who were brothers, so I sold one of them. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: What happened to the two boys? I said: I sold one of them. He said: Return him."
"182","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Fadalh narrated to us, from al-Hasan, he said: al-Ahnaf ibn Qays informed me, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made peace with Quraysh, he wrote: This is what Muhammad, the Messenger of Allah, has agreed upon. They said: Had we known you were the Messenger of Allah, we would not have fought you. So he erased it and wrote: Muhammad ibn Abd Allah."
"183","Abu Dawud said: Qays narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from al-Sha'bi, from Abd Allah ibn Khalil al-Hadrami, from Ali (may Allah be pleased with him), that he was brought three men who had shared in one woman's purity, so he cast lots among them and said: You are contentious partners. He assigned the child to the one who won the lot, and assigned for the other two two-thirds of the blood money. That was reported to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he laughed until his molars appeared."
"184","Abu Dawud said: Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Habbah al-Urani, he said: I heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) delivering a sermon, and he laughed a laugh the like of which I never saw him laugh, while upon the pulpit. He said: I saw myself praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). My father looked in on us while I was praying with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and said: O my son, what were you two doing? I said: We were praying. Abu Talib said: By Allah, by Allah, my backside shall never rise above me. I saw him laughing at his father's statement. Then he said: I saw myself having prayed before the people for years."
"185","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah al-Dabbi, from Umm Musa, she said: I heard Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I have neither suffered eye inflammation nor headache since the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) handed me the banner on the day of Khaybar."
"186","Abu Dawud said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Fakhita, he said: Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited us and spent the night with us, while al-Hasan and al-Husayn were sleeping. Al-Hasan asked for water, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went to a waterskin of ours and began squeezing it into a cup, then giving him to drink. Al-Husayn reached out to drink, but he prevented him and began with al-Hasan. Fatimah said: O Messenger of Allah, it is as if he is dearer to you. He said: No, but he asked for water first. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I, and you, and these two - and I think he said: and this one sleeping - meaning Ali - will be in one place on the Day of Resurrection."
"187","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Jami' ibn Shaddad informed me, he said: Amir ibn Abd Allah ibn al-Zubayr informed me, from his father, he said: I said to al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with them both): What prevents you from narrating from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Ibn Mas'ud and so-and-so narrate? He said: By Allah, I have not parted from him since I embraced Islam, but I heard him say a statement. He said: Whoever says about me what I did not say, let him take his seat in Hell."
"188","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muslim ibn Jundub, from al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We used to pray Jumu'ah with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then we would hasten to the shade, and there would be nothing but the space of a foot or two feet."
"189","Abu Dawud said: al-Salt ibn Dinar narrated to us, he said: Uqbah ibn Suhban and Abu Raja' al-Utaridi narrated to us, they said: We heard al-Zubayr (may Allah be pleased with him) reciting this verse: {And fear a trial which will not strike only those who have wronged among you}. He said: I recited this verse for a time and did not consider myself among its people, yet we have become among its people."
"190","Abu Dawud said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, that Ya'ish ibn al-Walid ibn Hisham narrated to him that a freedman of al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to him that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There has crept to you the disease of the nations before you: envy and hatred. Hatred is the shaver; I do not say it shaves the hair, but it shaves the religion. By the One in whose hand is my soul, you will not enter Paradise until you believe, and you will not believe until you love one another. Shall I not inform you of what will establish that for you: Spread salaam among yourselves."
"191","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami, from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me while I was ill, and said to me: Have you made a bequest? I said: Yes, I have bequeathed all my wealth. He said: Then what have you left for your children? I said: They are rich with good. He said: Bequeath a tenth. He kept reducing me and I kept reducing until he said: Bequeath a third, and a third is much."
"192","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah and others narrated to us, all from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I fell ill with an illness from which I nearly died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, I have much wealth, and only one daughter inherits from me. Should I give all my wealth in charity? He said: No. I said: Should I give half in charity - or he said: should I bequeath half? He said: No. I said: O Messenger of Allah, then of what should I bequeath? He said: A third, and a third is much. For you to leave your heirs rich is better than to leave them dependent begging from people's hands."
"193","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah and others narrated to us, all from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You never spend an expenditure but you are rewarded for it, even the morsel you raise to your wife's mouth."
"194","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd and Abd al-Aziz ibn Abi Salamah and others narrated to us, all from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, he said: I fell severely ill and nearly died. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon me, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, will I be left behind without my Hijrah? He said: You will not be left behind after me and perform a deed seeking Allah's face but you will increase thereby in rank and degree. Perhaps you will be left behind until some people benefit through you and other people are harmed through you. O Allah, complete for my Companions their Hijrah, and do not turn them back on their heels. But the wretched one is Sa'd ibn Khawlah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) felt pity for him that he died in Makkah."
"195","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Amir ibn Sa'd, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave to some people and withheld from a man. Sa'd said: O Messenger of Allah, by Allah, he is indeed a believer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. Sa'd then said: By Allah, I see him as a believer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Or a Muslim. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I give to a man and leave one who is better than him, fearing that Allah Almighty will throw him face down into Hell."
"196","Abu Dawud said: Thabit Abu Zayd and Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: My ears heard and my heart retained from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Whoever claims sonship to other than his father, knowing he is other than his father, Paradise is forbidden to him."
"197","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Ziyad ibn Mikhraq informed me, he said: I heard Abu Abayah - or Qays ibn Abayah, Abu Dawud doubted - that Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) heard a son of his saying: O Allah, I ask You for Paradise, its chambers such and such, and I seek refuge in You from Hell and its shackles and chains. Sa'd said to him: You have asked Allah for much good, and sought refuge in Him from much evil - or he said: great - and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There will be a people who transgress in supplication. It suffices you to say: O Allah, I ask You for all good, what I know of it and what I do not know, and I seek refuge in You from all evil, what I know of it and what I do not know."
"198","Abu Dawud said: Sa'id ibn Hassan al-Makki narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Mulaykah, from Ubayd Allah ibn Abi Nahik, from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: He is not of us who does not chant the Qur'an melodiously."
"199","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Yunus ibn Jubayr narrating from Muhammad ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For the belly of the son of Adam to be filled with pus is better for him than to be filled with poetry."
"200","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Qatadah, he said: I heard Ikrimah ibn Khalid al-Makhzumi narrating from Ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning the plague: If it is in a land and you are in it, do not leave it; and if it is in a land and you are not in it, do not enter it. Abu Dawud said: Whoever says other than this has erred."
"201","Abu Dawud said: Salim ibn Hayyan narrated to us, he said: Ikrimah ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"202","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, he said: I heard Ibrahim ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrating from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa."
"203","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, from Sa'd, he said: I saw on the day of Uhud, on the right of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and on his left, two men wearing white garments, fighting on behalf of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the fiercest fighting. I never saw them before that day nor after it."
"204","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, he heard Mus'ab ibn Sa'd saying: I prayed beside Sa'd. When I bowed, I joined my hands together and placed them between my knees. My father said to me: We used to do that until we were forbidden from it, and we were commanded to place our hands upon the knees."
"205","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb informed me, he said: I heard Mus'ab ibn Sa'd saying: Four verses were revealed concerning my father. He said: My father said: I acquired a sword on the day of Badr, so I brought it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, grant it to me as spoils. He said: Put it back where you took it. Then I returned to him and said: Shall I be left like one who has no benefit? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it back where you took it. Then this verse was revealed: {They ask you about the spoils} - and in Abd Allah's recitation it is thus: (They ask you about the spoils) - the whole verse. He said: Sa'd's mother said: Has Allah not commanded obedience to parents? So I shall not eat food nor drink drink until you disbelieve in Allah. She abstained from food and drink until they began propping her mouth open with a stick. Then was revealed: {And We have enjoined upon man goodness to his parents, but if they strive to make you associate with Me what you have no knowledge of, do not obey them}. A man of the Ansar made food and invited some of the Muhajirun and some of the Ansar. We ate and drank until we became intoxicated, then we boasted. A man raised a camel's jawbone and split Sa'd's nose with it, so Sa'd was left with a split nose, and that was before wine was forbidden. Then was revealed: {O you who believe, do not approach prayer while intoxicated} and was revealed: {Wine and gambling and idols and divining arrows are but defilement from the work of Satan} - the verse. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered upon Sa'd while he was ill, and he wanted to bequeath all his wealth, so he kept reducing him until it reached a third. He said: So people bequeath a third."
"206","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from Sa'd, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left Ali ibn Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) behind in the expedition of Tabuk. He said: O Messenger of Allah, do you leave me behind among the women and children? He said: Are you not pleased to be to me as Harun was to Musa, except that there is no Prophet after me."
"207","Abu Dawud said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd al-Ansari narrated to us, he said: Isma'il ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas narrated to me, from his father, from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three things are of the happiness of the son of Adam, and three things are of the wretchedness of the son of Adam. Of the happiness of the son of Adam are: a righteous wife, a sound mount, and a spacious dwelling - or he said: and a righteous dwelling. And of the wretchedness of the son of Adam are three: an evil dwelling, an evil wife, and an evil mount."
"208","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Ayzar ibn Hurayth narrating from Umar ibn Sa'd, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: I am amazed at the Muslim; when a calamity befalls him he seeks reward and is patient, and when good befalls him he praises Allah and is grateful. The Muslim is rewarded in everything, even in the morsel he raises to his mouth."
"209","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Abi Khalid, from Qays ibn Abi Hazim, he said: I heard Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I saw us with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when we had no food but tree leaves, until one of us would relieve himself like the sheep relieve themselves. Now Banu Asad reproach me concerning Islam. I would indeed have lost then and my striving would have gone astray."
"210","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn Zayd, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to Ali (may Allah be pleased with him): You are to me as Harun was to Musa."
"211","Abu Dawud said: Malik ibn Anas narrated to us, from Abd Allah ibn Yazid, from Zayd Abu Ayyash, he said: I asked Sa'd about buying sult grain with white wheat, and he disliked it. Sa'd said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about fresh dates for dried dates. He said: Does the fresh date decrease when it dries? They said: Yes. He said: No - or: he forbade it."
"212","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah, Hisham, and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us - all of them - from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Mus'ab ibn Sa'd, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which people are tried most severely? He said: The Prophets, then the next best, then the next best, until a man is tried according to his religion. If he is firm in religion, his trial is severe; and if there is softness in his religion, he is tried according to that - or: to that measure. Trial does not leave the servant until he walks upon the earth with no sin upon him."
"213","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Awn al-Thaqafi, he said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: Umar said to Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him): They have complained about you in everything, even in the prayer. He said: As for me, I used to prolong the first two rak'ahs and shorten the last two, and I do not fall short of what I followed of the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: That is what is thought of you, or: my thought of you."
"214","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr, from Jabir ibn Samurah, he said: The people of Kufah complained about Sa'd to Umar, so he removed him and appointed Ammar over them. They said: Sa'd does not know how to pray well. Umar mentioned that to him. Sa'd said: As for me, I used to lead them in the prayer of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and I did not deviate from it: the two evening prayers; I lingered in the first two and shortened in the last two. Umar said: That is what is thought of you, O Abu Ishaq."
"215","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Salih, freedman of al-Taw'amah, he said: One of Sa'd's children narrated to me, from Sa'd, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whomever you catch cutting anything of the trees - meaning the trees of the sanctuary - his spoils belong to you. Its trees shall not be lopped, nor cut. He said: Sa'd saw some youths cutting, so he took their goods. They went to their masters and informed them that Sa'd did such and such. They came to him and said: O Abu Ishaq, your youths - or: your freedmen - took our youths' goods. He said: Rather I took them. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whomever you catch cutting of the trees of the sanctuary, his spoils belong to you. But ask me from my wealth whatever you wish."
"216","Abu Dawud said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib, from Sa'd ibn Malik (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) refused Uthman ibn Maz'un celibacy, and had he permitted him it, we would have castrated ourselves."
"217","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, he said: I heard Sa'id ibn al-Musayyib saying: I heard Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) joined for me both his parents on the day of Uhud."
"218","Abu Dawud said: Isa ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'd, he said: There is no death by which I die dearer to me than to be killed defending my wealth while wronged."
"219","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Simak, he said: A man narrated to me, from his uncle Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him), that Banu Najiyah were mentioned before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he said: They are a clan of mine. He said: And I think he said: And I am of them. Either the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said it, or the man said that and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) answered him."
"220","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from his grandfather, that when Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf had led the prayer and the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came, he began to step back, so the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gestured to him: Stay as you are. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed following Abd al-Rahman's prayer."
"221","Abu Dawud said: Nasr ibn Ali al-Huddani narrated to us, he said: al-Nadr ibn Shayban narrated to us, he said: I met Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman, and said: Narrate to me a hadith your father narrated to you from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: My father narrated to me (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned Ramadan and said: A month whose fasting Allah has made obligatory upon you, and I have established its standing in prayer. Whoever fasts it and stands it in faith and seeking reward emerges from his sins like the day his mother bore him."
"222","Abu Dawud said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Dinar, from Bajalah, he said: Umar did not take jizyah from the Magians until Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with him) testified that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took it from the Magians of Hajar."
"223","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Abu al-Bakhtari, he said: I heard a hadith from a man and it pleased me, so I said: Write it down. He brought it to me written, inscribed. He said: Ali and al-Abbas entered upon Umar, and with him were Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf, al-Zubayr ibn al-Awwam, and Sa'd ibn Abi Waqqas. He said: I adjure you by Allah, did you not hear, did you not know, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: All the wealth of the Prophet is charity except what he fed his family and clothed them with. We are not inherited from. They said: Yes."
"224","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Bashshar ibn Abi Sayf, from al-Walid ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Ghudayf ibn al-Harith, he said: I heard Abu Ubaydah (may Allah be pleased with him) saying: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever spends a surplus expenditure in the path of Allah Almighty, the good deed is multiplied seven hundredfold. Whoever spends upon himself, or upon his family, or visits a sick person, or removes harm, the good deed is ten times its like. Fasting is a shield so long as he does not tear it. Whoever Allah Almighty afflicts in his body, for him is an expiation."
"225","Abu Dawud said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from Layth, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Sabit, from Abu Tha'labah al-Khushani, from Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah and Mu'adh ibn Jabal (may Allah be pleased with them), from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Allah Almighty began this matter as Prophethood and mercy, and there shall be caliphate and mercy, and there shall be biting kingship, and there shall be force and tyranny and corruption in the land. They will deem private parts, wines, and silk lawful, and will be aided upon that, and provided for ever, until they meet Allah."
"226","Abu Dawud said: Qays narrated to us, from Ibrahim ibn Maymun, from Ibn Samurah, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Expel the Jews of the Hijaz from the Arabian Peninsula."
"227","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I was with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he passed by people pollinating date palms. He said: What are these doing? I said: They are pollinating the palms, placing the male into the female. He said: I do not think this avails anything. Then he said: If it benefits them, let them do it. Do not hold me to account for opinion, but when I tell you something from Allah Almighty, I never lie about Allah at all."
"228","Abu Dawud said: Sallam and Yazid ibn Ata' narrated to us, from Simak, from Musa ibn Talhah, from his father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We mentioned one day to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) what passes before us of beasts while we pray. He said: Let one of you place before him something like the back of a saddle, and whatever passes before him will not harm him."
"229","Abu Dawud said: Sufyan narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, from a shaykh of theirs, from Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about game meat gifted by one in ihram-free state to one in ihram, and he permitted it."
"230","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from his father, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Muhammad ibn Ammar ibn Yasir, from Talhah ibn Abd Allah ibn Awf, from Sa'id ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr, and whoever is killed defending his blood is a martyr."
"231","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Nufayl ibn Hisham ibn Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl al-Adawi - Adi of Quraysh - from his father, from his grandfather, that Zayd ibn Amr and Waraqah ibn Nawfal went out seeking the religion until they reached a monk at Mosul. He said to Zayd ibn Amr: From where have you come, O rider of the camel? He said: From the house of Ibrahim. He said: And what do you seek? He said: I seek the religion. He said: Return, for the one you seek is about to appear in your land. As for Waraqah, he became Christian. Zayd said: As for me, Christianity was presented to me and it did not suit me. So he returned, saying: Truly, truly, righteousness. And he says: However much You burden me, then he falls down prostrating. He said: His son came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, my father was as you saw and as reached you, so seek forgiveness for him. He said: Yes, for he shall be a nation alone on the Day of Resurrection. He said: Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl came upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), with Zayd ibn Harithah, while they were eating from a dining mat of theirs, and they invited him to their food. Zayd ibn Amr said to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): O son of my brother, we do not eat of what is slaughtered upon idols."
"232","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Husayn ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, he said: I heard Hilal ibn Yasaf narrating from Abd Allah ibn Zalim al-Mazini, from Sa'id ibn Zayd (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon Hira, with Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with them). He said: Be firm, O Hira, for upon you is only a Prophet, or a truthful one, or a martyr. Sa'id mentioned that he was with them."
"233","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hurr ibn al-Sayyah al-Nakha'i, he said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Akhnas saying: I witnessed al-Mughirah ibn Shu'bah delivering a sermon, and he disparaged Ali. Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl al-Adawi - Adi of Quraysh - (may Allah be pleased with him) stood and said: I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Ten are in Paradise: the Messenger of Allah, Abu Bakr, Umar, Uthman, Ali, Talhah, al-Zubayr, Sa'd ibn Malik, and Abd al-Rahman ibn Awf (may Allah be pleased with them). Had I wished to name the tenth, I would name him. Then he named him, saying: Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"234","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith ibn Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Salamah, he said: Marwan sent us to reconcile between Sa'id ibn Zayd ibn Amr ibn Nufayl and a woman called Arwa, who claimed something of land against him. Sa'id said: Do you think I took anything of her land, when I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever wrongfully takes a handspan of land will be collared with it from seven earths."
"235","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from Sa'id (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever seizes wealth by his oath, Allah will not bless it for him."
"236","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd ibn Qunfudh, from Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn Talhah ibn Ubayd Allah, from Sa'id ibn Zayd, he said: Marwan wanted to take his land, but he refused him, and said: If they come to me, I shall fight them. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever is killed defending his wealth is a martyr."
"237","Abu Dawud said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Harith, from Abu Salamah, from Sa'id, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever takes as patron a freedman without the permission of his patrons, upon him is the curse of Allah."
"238","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: I asked Sa'd ibn Ibrahim about Banu Najiyah. He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They are a clan of mine, and I think he said: And I am of them. I said: Who narrates this from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? He said: Sa'id ibn Zayd."
"239","Abu Dawud said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far al-Jufri narrated to us, from Abu Thifal - of the people of Madinah - from Ibn Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza, from his grandmother, from her father (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: He has not believed in Allah who has not believed in me, and he has not believed in me who does not love the Ansar."
"240","Abu Dawud said: al-Hasan ibn Abi Ja'far narrated to us, from Abu Thifal, from Ibn Huwaytib ibn Abd al-Uzza, from his grandmother, from her father, he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: There is no prayer without wudu, and no wudu for one who does not mention Allah's name over it."
"241","Yunus said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) drew a line for us and said: This is Allah's path. Then he drew lines to its right and its left, and said: These are paths; upon each path among them is a devil calling to it. Then he recited: {And that this is My straight path} - the verse."
"242","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and greeted him, but he did not return it to me. I was seized by distress, old and new. I said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred concerning me? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty reveals to His Prophet of His affair what He wills, and among what He has newly revealed is that you shall not speak in prayer."
"243","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: Allah Almighty looked into the hearts of the servants and chose Muhammad, so He sent him with His messages and selected him with His knowledge. Then He looked into the hearts of the people after him and chose for him his Companions, making them supporters of His religion and ministers of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Whatever the believers deem good is good with Allah, and whatever the believers deem evil is evil with Allah."
"244","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The servant continues to speak truth and seek truth until he is recorded with Allah as a truthful one. And he continues to lie and seek lies until he is recorded with Allah as a liar."
"245","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Zubayd, he said: When the Murji'ah appeared, I came to Abu Wa'il and mentioned that to him. He said: I heard Abd Allah saying from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Abusing a believer is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"246","Abu Dawud said: Hisham narrated to us, from Hammad, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: When we prayed behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), we used to say: Peace be upon Allah, peace be upon Jibril, peace be upon Mika'il. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) turned to us and said: Do not say: Peace be upon Allah, for Allah Almighty is al-Salam. But say: Greetings belong to Allah, prayers and pure words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon Allah's righteous servants. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"247","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, he said: Abu Nahshal informed me, from Abu Wa'il, he said: Ibn Mas'ud said: Umar surpassed the people through the supplication of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning Umar: O Allah, strengthen the people through Umar."
"248","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, he said: Ibn al-Nawwahah and Ibn Uthal came as two messengers of Musaylimah to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Do you bear witness that I am Allah's Messenger? They said: We bear witness that Musaylimah is Allah's messenger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I believe in Allah and His messengers. Had I been one to kill a messenger, I would have killed you two. Abd Allah said: So the Sunnah continued that messengers are not killed. Abd Allah said: As for Ibn Uthal, Allah sufficed us against him; and as for Ibn al-Nawwahah, he remained in my mind until Allah Almighty gave power over him."
"249","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: Allah Almighty took Ibrahim as a close friend, and your Companion is Allah's close friend. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is the noblest of creation with Allah Almighty on the Day of Resurrection. Then he recited: {It may be that your Lord will raise you to a praised station}."
"250","Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us idle talk after the Isha prayer."
"251","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A person is with whom he loves."
"252","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: Every treacherous one shall have a banner on the Day of Resurrection; it shall be said: This is the treachery of so-and-so."
"253","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he heard Abu Wa'il saying: Abd Allah said: I am informed of your gathering, and nothing prevents me from coming out to you but fear of boring you. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to choose the right time to admonish us, fearing weariness for us."
"254","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said one statement, and I say another. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever dies while ascribing a rival to Allah enters Hell. Abd Allah said: And I say: Whoever dies while not ascribing a rival to Allah, Allah admits him to Paradise."
"255","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: When there are three, two shall not converse privately to the exclusion of the third, for that grieves him."
"256","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash and Mansur narrated to me, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Abusing a Muslim is wickedness, and fighting him is disbelief."
"257","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il saying: A man asked Abd Allah about Allah Almighty's statement {from water unaltered} or {Ya Sin}. Abd Allah said: Have you recited all the Qur'an except this? He said: Yes. He said: Some people recite it, scattering it like the scattering of inferior dates; it does not pass beyond their collarbones. I know the similar surahs which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pair together. He said: So we commanded Alqamah, and he asked him. He said: Twenty surahs of the Mufassal; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pair every two surahs in one rak'ah."
"258","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, he said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, shall we be taken to account for what we did in Jahiliyyah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever does good in Islam will not be taken to account for what he did in Jahiliyyah and Islam. Whoever does evil in Islam will be taken to account for what he did in Jahiliyyah and Islam."
"259","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: How evil it is for one of them to say: I forgot such and such verse. Rather, he was made to forget. Keep recalling the Qur'an, for by the One in whose hand is my soul, it escapes from men's chests more swiftly than camels from their hobbles."
"260","Abu Dawud said: Warqa' narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, he said: Whoever swears a binding oath to seize thereby wealth, being wicked in it, shall meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him. He said: al-Ash'ath ibn Qays al-Kindi came out to us and said: What did Abu Abd al-Rahman narrate to you? He said: So we said: Such and such hadith. He said: He spoke the truth; it was revealed concerning me. I disputed with a man about a well before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your proof, or his oath. I said: Then he will swear while sinful. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever swears a binding oath, being wicked or sinful in it, to seize thereby wealth, shall meet Allah Almighty while He is angry with him. And was revealed: {Those who purchase with Allah's covenant and their oaths a small price} - the verse."
"261","Abu Dawud said: Warqa' narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah - Abu Dawud said: I think he raised it - he said: Before the Hour are days of harj: days in which knowledge departs and ignorance appears. Al-Ash'ari was beside Ibn Mas'ud, and al-Ash'ari said: Harj means killing."
"262","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: Wasil informed me, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, he said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which sin is greatest? He said: That you ascribe a rival to Allah while He created you. He said: Then which? He said: That you kill your child lest he share your wealth. He said: Then which? He said: That you commit adultery with your neighbor's wife."
"263","Abu Dawud said: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it, and he recited this verse: {And those who do not invoke with Allah another god, nor kill the soul which Allah has forbidden except by right, nor commit adultery}."
"264","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, he heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, he said: I said: Did you hear it from him and did he raise it? He said: Yes. He said: No one is more jealous than Allah Almighty, and therefore He forbade indecencies, what is apparent of them and what is hidden. None loves praise more than Allah, and therefore He praised Himself. And no one loves excuses more than Allah, Blessed and Exalted."
"265","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr, and he heard Abu Wa'il narrating that a man came to Ibn Mas'ud and said: I recited the Mufassal tonight in one rak'ah. Abd Allah said: Like the hasty recitation of poetry! I know the similar surahs which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pair together. He mentioned twenty surahs of the Mufassal, two surahs in one rak'ah."
"266","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: A woman shall not touch another woman and then describe her to her husband, as if he is looking at her."
"267","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The first thing judged - or: decreed - among people on the Day of Resurrection is bloodshed."
"268","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash said to me: Shall I not narrate to you a fine hadith? Ibrahim narrated to me, he said: Alqamah narrated to me, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, he said: When was revealed: {Those who believe and have not mixed their faith with wrong}, they said: Which of us has not erred? Until this verse was revealed: {Do not associate with Allah; indeed association is a great wrong}."
"269","Abu Dawud said: Za'idah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and added or omitted - the one who forgot that is either Ibrahim from Alqamah, or Alqamah from Abd Allah. When he finished his prayer, it was said: O Messenger of Allah, has something new occurred in the prayer? He said: No, and what is that? We mentioned to him what he had done. He folded his leg, faced the qiblah, then prostrated two prostrations. Then he turned to us with his face and said: Had something new occurred in the prayer, I would have informed you. But I am a human like you; I forget as you forget. When I forget, remind me. Whichever of you doubts in his prayer, let him seek what is closest to correctness and complete upon it. Then let him give salaam, and prostrate two prostrations."
"270","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, that he was standing with Abd Allah at Arafah in Uthman's caliphate. Uthman said to Abd Allah: Shall I not marry you - Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah or another said in this chain: Shall I not marry you to a slave girl who will remind you of yourself what you have forgotten? He said: Abd Allah said so as to make Alqamah hear: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Whoever among you can afford marriage, let him marry; otherwise let him fast, for fasting is a restraint for him."
"271","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abu Wa'il saying: Abd Allah said: I know the similar surahs which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pair together. He said: So we commanded Alqamah, and he asked him. He said: Twenty surahs of the Mufassal; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to pair every two surahs in one rak'ah."
"272","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Mughirah, from Ibrahim, from Hunayy ibn Nuwayrah, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: The most restrained of people in killing are the people of faith."
"273","Abu Dawud said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn al-Hurr, from al-Qasim ibn Mukhaymirah, he said: Alqamah took my hand, and Alqamah mentioned that Ibn Mas'ud took his hand, and Ibn Mas'ud mentioned that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took his hand and taught him the tashahhud: Greetings belong to Allah, prayers and pure words. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and Allah's mercy and blessings. Peace be upon us and upon Allah's righteous servants. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger. When you say that, your prayer is complete. If you wish, stand; and if you wish, sit."
"274","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he prayed Zuhr five rak'ahs. It was said to him: Has the prayer been increased? The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And what is that? They said: You prayed five. So he prostrated two prostrations after he gave salaam."
"275","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reclined upon a mat, and the mat left marks on his skin. I began wiping it from him, saying: May my father and mother be ransomed for you, O Messenger of Allah, will you not permit us to spread for you something to protect you, to sleep upon? He said: What have I to do with the world? I and the world are but like a rider who shades himself beneath a tree, then departs and leaves it."
"276","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Alqamah, from Abd Allah, concerning His Almighty's statement: {He certainly saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. He said: He saw Jibril (peace be upon him) upon a green carpet, having covered the horizon of the sky."
"277","Abu Dawud said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, and Alqamah, from Abd Allah, he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying takbir in every lowering and rising, standing and sitting, and giving salaam to his right and to his left, until I saw the whiteness of his cheek. And I saw Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) doing that."
"278","Abu Dawud said: Yazid ibn Ata' narrated to us, from Simak, from Ibrahim al-Nakha'i, from Alqamah or al-Aswad, from Abd Allah, concerning Allah Almighty's statement {The Hour has drawn near and the moon has split}. He said: The moon split in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"279","Abu Dawud said: Wuhayb ibn Khalid and Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Sha'bi, from Alqamah, he said: I said to Ibn Mas'ud: People say that you were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of the jinn. He said: None of us accompanied him, but we missed him in Makkah and sought him in the mountain passes and valleys. I said: He has been assassinated, snatched away. We spent the worst night ever spent by a people. When morning came, we saw him approaching. We said: O Messenger of Allah, last night we spent the worst night ever spent by a people; we missed you. He said: A caller of the jinn came to me, so I went and recited the Qur'an to them. He took us along and showed us their dwellings and their fires. They asked him for provision, and he said: Every bone over which Allah's name has not been mentioned, falling into your hands at its meatiest, and every dung is fodder for your beasts. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade us to cleanse ourselves with them, and said: It is the provision of your brothers among the jinn."
"280","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Aswad, he heard Abd Allah: He heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting {Is there then any who will remember}."
"281","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: I heard al-Aswad ibn Yazid narrating from Abd Allah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) recited al-Najm in Makkah and prostrated in it, and those with him prostrated, except an old man who took a handful of pebbles or dust, raised it to his forehead, and said: This suffices me. Abd Allah said: I saw him killed as a disbeliever on the day of Badr."
"282","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr narrating from al-Aswad, from Abd Allah, he said: Let none of you assign to Satan a portion of his prayer, deeming it binding upon him not to leave except to his right. I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaving most often to his left."
"283","Abu Dawud said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, he said: Simak ibn Harb narrated to us, from Ibrahim, from al-Aswad or Alqamah, from Abd Allah ibn Mas'ud, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that he had touched a woman short of intercourse. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not answer him until Allah Almighty revealed: {And establish prayer at the two ends of the day and at the approaches of the night} - the verse. A man said: O Messenger of Allah, is it for him specifically or for all people? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Rather for all people."
"284","Abu Dawud said: Hammam narrated to us, from Ata' ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abd Allah, that he used to give salaam to his right: Peace be upon you, and Allah's mercy and blessings; and to his left: Peace be upon you and Allah's mercy. It has been reported from al-Aswad, through other than this chain, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the like of it."
"285","Abu Dawud said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, he said: It was not Abu Ubaydah who narrated to me, but Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from Abd Allah, he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the lavatory, so I followed him. I placed for him two stones and a dung. He came out, took the two stones, threw away the dung, and said: It is filth."
"286","Abu Dawud said: Shayban narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, from his father, from Abd Allah, that when captives were brought to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he would give the whole household together, disliking to separate them."
"287","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Murrah narrating from Masruq, from Abd Allah, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The blood of a Muslim man is not lawful except by one of three: the married adulterer, a life for a life, and one who abandons his religion, separating from the community."
"288","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abd Allah ibn Murrah - I think from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Abu Dawud said: Za'idah said in this chain, from Abd Allah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he said: He is not of us who strikes the cheeks, tears the garments, and calls with the call of Jahiliyyah."
"289","Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah narrated to us, he said: al-A'mash informed me, he said: I heard Abd Allah ibn Murrah narrating from Masruq, he said: We asked Abd Allah about the souls of the martyrs - and were it not for Abd Allah, we would find no one to narrate to us - and he said: The souls of the martyrs are with Allah in the crops of green birds, roaming in the rivers of Paradise wherever they wish, then sheltering to lamps beneath the Throne. Their Lord Almighty says to them: What do you desire? They say: We desire nothing - saying it three times - except to be returned to the world and killed."
"290","Abu Dawud said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Jabir, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abd Allah, he said: I bear witness upon the truthful, confirmed Abu al-Qasim (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that he said: Selling muhaffalat animals is deceit, and deceit is not lawful for a Muslim."
"291","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, that when Quraysh became defiant toward the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), he supplicated against them for years of famine until they ate carrion and bones, until a man would stand and see between himself and the sky something like smoke; that is His Almighty saying: {On the Day when the sky will bring a clear smoke}."
"292","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: Whoever has knowledge, let him speak with his knowledge, and whoever does not have knowledge - or he said: whoever is asked about what he has no knowledge of - let him say: Allah knows best, for Allah Almighty said to His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): {Say: I do not ask you for any reward except love for kin}."
"293","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from al-Mughirah, from Abu al-Duha, from Masruq, from Abdullah, who said: The moon split in the lifetime of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), so Quraysh said: This is the magic of Ibn Abi Kabshah. He said: And they said: Wait for what the travellers bring to you, for Muhammad cannot bewitch all the people. He said: Then the travellers came and reported the same."
"294","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Yahya ibn Waththab, from Masruq, from Abdullah, raising it to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The impure does not expiate the evil deed, but the pure expiates the evil deed."
"295","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb narrating from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will see after me favoritism and matters which you will disapprove of. We said: O Messenger of Allah, what do you command us? He said: Render to them their right which He has granted them, and ask Allah for your right."
"296","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb al-Juhani saying: I heard Abdullah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us, and he is the truthful, the believed: The creation of one of you is gathered in his mother's womb for forty nights, then he becomes a clot for the like of that, then he becomes a lump of flesh for the like of that, then an angel is sent to him and commanded with four words: his provision, his lifespan, his deed, and whether wretched or happy; then the soul is breathed into him. By Allah, one of you - or a man among you - may do the deeds of the people of Paradise until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the decree overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Hellfire and enters it; and a man among you - or one of you - may do the deeds of the people of Hellfire until there is only a cubit between him and it, then the decree overtakes him and he does the deeds of the people of Paradise and enters it."
"297","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur and al-A'mash, from Ibrahim, from Abidah al-Salmani, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The best of my nation are my generation, then those who follow them, then those who follow them; then there will come a people whose oaths will precede their testimony, and they will testify before they are asked to testify."
"298","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq informed me, who said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Had I taken a close friend from my nation, I would have taken Abu Bakr."
"299","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq informed me, who said: I heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from Abdullah, who said: Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man speaks the truth until he is recorded as a truthful one, and a man lies until he is recorded as a liar."
"300","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq informed me, who heard Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: We came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning a companion of ours, seeking his permission to cauterize him, and he remained silent; then we asked him again and he remained silent; then we asked him a third time and he remained silent; then we asked him again and he said: Brand him with hot stones, burn him - and he disliked that."
"301","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to supplicate with this supplication: O Allah, I ask You for guidance, piety, chastity, and sufficiency."
"302","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, who heard Abu al-Ahwas, who said: Abdullah said: We did not know what to say in every two rak'ahs except to glorify, magnify, and praise our Lord, and Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was taught the openings of good and its comprehensive phrases - or its comprehensive and concluding phrases - and he commanded us to say in every two rak'ahs: Greetings belong to Allah, and prayers and good words; peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah and His blessings; peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah; I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger; then let one of you choose the supplication most pleasing to him and supplicate with it."
"303","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I came to al-Aswad ibn Yazid - and he was a brother and friend to me - and I said: Abu al-Ahwas adds in the tashahhud from Abdullah: and the blessed ones. He said: Go to him and forbid him from this, and tell him: Abdullah taught Alqamah the tashahhud, counting them on his hand."
"304","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who heard Abu al-Ahwas narrating from Abdullah, who said: Indeed Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fighting a Muslim is disbelief, and abusing him is wickedness; and it is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days."
"305","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd al-Abdi, from Abu al-A'yan, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: We asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about monkeys and pigs, whether they are from the offspring of the Jews. He said: No; Allah Almighty never cursed a people and transformed them and then gave them offspring; rather this was a creation that already existed, but when Allah Almighty became angry with the Jews and transformed them, He made them like them."
"306","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) gave the greeting of peace in the prayer with two salutations."
"307","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Humayd al-Kindi - or al-Abdi - from al-Jarud, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not revile Quraysh, for their learned one will fill the earth with knowledge. O Allah, You made the first of them taste torment - or calamity - so make the last of them taste bounty."
"308","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ja'far narrated to us, from al-Nadr ibn Humayd, from al-Jarud, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the broad forearms of one who sheds blood impress you, for he has with Allah a killer who does not die; and let not a man who earned wealth unlawfully impress you, for if he spends it or gives it in charity it will not be accepted from him, and if he leaves it, it will not be blessed for him in it, and if any of it remains it will be his provision to the Fire."
"309","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: The Hour will not come except upon the worst of people."
"310","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Ibrahim al-Hajari, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: When Allah gives you wealth, let it be seen upon you; give from the surplus, begin with those you support, and you are not blamed for sufficiency. Hands are three: the Hand of Allah Almighty is the highest, the hand of the giver which follows it, and the hand of the beggar which is the lowest until the Day of Resurrection. And other than Shu'bah raised it to the Prophet."
"311","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Ali ibn al-Aqmar, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: Whoever wishes to meet Allah Almighty tomorrow as a Muslim, let him guard these five prayers wherever the call is made for them, for Allah has legislated for your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) the ways of guidance, and they are among the ways of guidance. I do not think any of you but has a mosque in which he prays in his house; yet if you prayed in your houses and abandoned your mosques, you would have abandoned the practice of your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and if you abandoned the practice of your Prophet you would go astray. There is no Muslim who performs ablution well, then walks to the prayer, except that for every step he takes a good deed is written for him, he is raised a degree by it, and a sin is expiated from him by it, so much so that we used to shorten our steps. I have seen us, and none would stay behind from it except a hypocrite whose hypocrisy was known; I have even seen a man supported between two men until he was stood in the row."
"312","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Isma'il ibn Raja, from Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Had I taken a close friend, I would have taken Abu Bakr as a close friend; but he is my brother and my companion, and your companion is the close friend of Allah."
"313","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat narrated to us, from Muhammad ibn Zayd, from Abu al-A'yan, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Whoever kills a snake, it is as if he killed a disbeliever."
"314","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I intended to command a man to lead the people in prayer, then stay behind against people who stay behind from Friday prayer and burn their houses over them."
"315","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays ibn al-Rabi' narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: Indeed I am the Provider, Possessor of power, the Strong."
"316","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Umarah ibn Umayr, or another, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah, who said: I performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he prayed two rak'ahs at Mina; and with Abu Bakr, and he prayed two rak'ahs at Mina; and with Umar, and he prayed two rak'ahs. Would that my share of four rak'ahs were two accepted ones."
"317","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Ibrahim, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, that he performed Hajj with Abdullah and stoned the jamrah with seven pebbles, placing the House on his left and Mina on his right, and said: This is the standing place of the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"318","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, who said: We were on a campaign in which Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid was present, and it spread among the people that some disliked saying Surah al-Baqarah and Ali Imran, insisting on saying: the surah in which the cow is mentioned, and the surah in which Ali Imran is mentioned. Abd al-Rahman said: I was with Abdullah at Mina when he went to the bottom of the valley, placed the jamrah on his right eyebrow side, then faced the Ka'bah and stoned it with seven pebbles, magnifying Allah with each pebble. When he finished he said: From here - by the One besides whom there is no deity - stoned the one to whom Surah al-Baqarah was revealed."
"319","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, who said: Abdullah prayed the dawn prayer at Muzdalifah in the darkness before dawn, and said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would not pray this prayer at this time except in this place."
"320","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Hakim ibn Jubayr, from Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever begs while having sufficiency will come on the Day of Resurrection with scratches or gashes on his face. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, what suffices him? He said: Fifty dirhams or its value in gold."
"321","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, concerning His Almighty saying: {The heart did not lie about what it saw}, he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw Gabriel in a green brocade garment filling what is between heaven and earth."
"322","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq informed me, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in a dome, about forty of us, and he said: Are you pleased to be a quarter of the people of Paradise? They said: Yes. He said: Are you pleased to be a third of the people of Paradise? He said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, I hope you will be half of the people of Paradise; and that is because none will enter Paradise except a Muslim soul, and you among the polytheists are but like a white hair on the skin of a black bull, or like a black hair on the skin of a red bull."
"323","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, who said: I heard Amr ibn Maymun narrating from Abdullah, who said: While the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was prostrating with people of Quraysh around him, and there was the afterbirth of a camel nearby, they said: Who will take the afterbirth of this slaughtered camel - or camel - and throw it on the back of the Prophet? So Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt came and threw it on the back of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Then Fatimah came and took it from his back and supplicated against whoever did that. Abdullah said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) supplicate against them except that day, when he said: O Allah, upon You are the chiefs of Quraysh; O Allah, upon You are Abu Jahl ibn Hisham, Utbah ibn Rabi'ah, Shaybah ibn Rabi'ah, Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt, and Umayyah ibn Khalaf - or Ubayy ibn Khalaf - Shu'bah doubted. Abdullah said: I saw them killed on the day of Badr and thrown into the well - or he said: into a pit - except that Ubayy ibn Khalaf - or Umayyah ibn Khalaf - was a corpulent man, so he broke apart before being brought to the pit."
"324","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, who said: Muslim al-Batin narrated to us, from Amr ibn Maymun, who said: I frequented Abdullah ibn Mas'ud for a year, never hearing him say in it: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, except that one day a narration came up and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said - then distress overcame him and sweat began to pour from his eyes - then he said: something above that, or below that, or close to that."
"325","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would supplicate three times and seek forgiveness three times."
"326","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Waki' narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Amr ibn Maymun, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: On the day of Badr I came upon Abu Jahl while he was struck down; I struck him with my sword but it did nothing, and his sword fell, so I struck him again. Then I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a hot day as though lifted from the ground, and I said: O Messenger of Allah, this enemy of Allah, Abu Jahl, has been killed. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By Allah, has he indeed been killed? I said: By Allah, he has indeed been killed. So go with us and we showed him to him; he came to him, looked at him, and said: This was the Pharaoh of this nation."
"327","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Amr ibn Ja'dah, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that a man came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and asked him about the Night of Decree. He said: Which of you remembers the night of the moonlit nights? Abdullah said: I, by Allah - may my father and mother be sacrificed - remember it; there were in my hand some dates with which I was taking sahur, screened by the back of my saddle from the dawn, and that was when the moon was rising."
"328","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yazid ibn Ata narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, who said: The prophets used to ride donkeys, wear wool, and milk sheep; and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had a donkey named Ufayr."
"329","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Ibrahim, who said: I heard Abu Ubaydah narrating from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the first two rak'ahs was as though upon hot stones; he said: He would move his lips with something, so I say: until he stands, and he says: until he stands."
"330","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ubayd ibn Nistas, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: When one of you follows a funeral, let him take hold of all four sides of the bier, then volunteer afterwards or leave it, for it is from the practice."
"331","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Abu al-Zubayr, from Nafi' ibn Jubayr, from Abu Ubaydah, from his father, who said: The polytheists distracted us from the noon, afternoon, sunset, and night prayers, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded Bilal, who called the adhan and the iqamah, and we prayed noon; then he gave the iqamah and we prayed afternoon; then he gave the iqamah and we prayed sunset; then he gave the iqamah and we prayed night. Then he said: There is no band on earth remembering Allah Almighty besides you."
"332","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever wishes to recite the Qur'an fresh as it was revealed, let him recite it upon the recitation of Ibn Umm Abd."
"333","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sallam and Qays narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Ubaydah, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Have mercy on those on earth, and He who is in heaven will have mercy on you."
"334","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey when a man entered a thicket and took out the egg of a lark. The lark came fluttering over the head of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions, and he said: Which of you has bereaved this one? A man among the people said: I took its egg. He said: Return it, return it, out of mercy for her."
"335","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Simak ibn Harb informed me, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah ibn Mas'ud narrating from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: You will attain, be aided, and have conquests opened for you; whoever among you reaches that, let him fear Allah, enjoin good, and forbid evil."
"336","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, who said: I heard Abu Ubaydah ibn Abdullah narrating from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught us the sermon of need: All praise belongs to Allah - or: praise belongs to Allah - we seek His help and seek His forgiveness, and we seek refuge in Allah from the evils of our souls. Whomever Allah guides, none can misguide; and whomever He misguides, none can guide. I bear witness that there is no deity but Allah, and I bear witness that Muhammad is His servant and His Messenger. Then he would recite the three verses: {O you who believe, fear Allah as He deserves to be feared} to the end of the verse, and recite: {O people, fear your Lord who created you from a single soul} the verse, then recite: {O you who believe, fear Allah and speak upright words; He will amend your deeds for you} to the end of the verse. Then speak your need. Shu'bah said: I said to Abu Ishaq: Is this in the marriage sermon or otherwise? He said: In every need."
"337","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu Ubaydah narrating from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) would often say: Glory be to You, our Lord, and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me. When {When the help of Allah and the victory comes} and {So glorify with the praise of your Lord and seek His forgiveness; indeed He is the Accepter of repentance} were revealed, he said: Glory be to You and with Your praise; O Allah, forgive me; indeed You are the Accepter of repentance, the Merciful."
"338","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Abu Ubaydah narrating from his father, who said: While I was praying one night, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), Abu Bakr, and Umar passed by me, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ask, you will be given. Umar said: So Abu Bakr and I raced; never did I race Abu Bakr to any good but I found he had preceded me to it. Then I set out and said: I have a supplication I hardly ever abandon: O Allah, I ask You for faith that does not turn back, coolness of the eye that does not cease - or he said: that does not perish - and the companionship of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the highest garden of eternity."
"339","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, who said: I entered the mosque of Kufah on Friday and there was a man around whom people had gathered; had they been able to take him into their bellies they would have, out of their love for him; and he was narrating. He said: Abdullah said: Do not say often of martyrdom: so-and-so was killed a martyr, and so-and-so was killed a martyr; but if you must praise a people that they were martyred, then praise a detachment the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent to a tribe, and hardly a short while passed before the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and said: Indeed your brothers have met their Lord; and they asked Allah Almighty to convey from them that they are pleased and He is pleased with them. So if you praise a people that they are martyrs, praise those. He said: And the man was Abu Ubaydah."
"340","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Simak informed me, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrating from his father, that he heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"341","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the consumer of usury, its payer, and its two witnesses - or he said: and its witness and its scribe."
"342","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah narrating from his father, who said: The likeness of one who aids his people in other than truth is like a camel that has fallen into a pit and is dragged by its tail. Amr ibn Thabit raised it to the Prophet, while Shu'bah did not raise it."
"343","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abdullah, from his father, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stopped at a place and went off for his need; he came back when a man had set fire to a village of ants, either in a tree or on the ground. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Who did this? A man among the people said: I did. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Put it out, put it out."
"344","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hudayj ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abdullah ibn Utbah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent us to the Negus, eighty men, with us Ja'far ibn Abi Talib and Uthman ibn Maz'un. Quraysh sent Umarah and Amr ibn al-As, and sent with them a gift to the Negus. When they entered upon him they prostrated to him and handed him the gift, saying: Some people of our tribe have turned away from our religion and have settled in your land. He said: Where are they? They said: They are in your land, so the Negus sent for them. Ja'far said: I am your spokesman today, so they followed him until they entered upon the Negus, but they did not prostrate to him. He said: Why do you not prostrate to the king? He said: Allah Almighty sent to us His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who commanded us not to prostrate except to Allah. The Negus said: What is that? So he was informed, and Amr ibn al-As said: They oppose you concerning Jesus. He said: What do you say concerning Jesus and his mother? He said: We say as Allah Almighty said: He is the Spirit of Allah and His Word, which He cast to the chaste virgin whom no man touched and to whom no child was attributed. So the Negus took a stick and said: O company of priests and monks, you do not exceed what these say by the weight of this. Welcome to you and to him from whom you have come; I bear witness that he is a prophet. I would love to be with him and carry his sandals - or he said: serve him. Settle wherever you wish in my land. Then Ibn Mas'ud came hastening and witnessed Badr."
"345","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abdullah ibn Utbah, from his father, from Abdullah, who said: We were with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he smiled. We said: O Messenger of Allah, at what did you smile? He said: I marvel at the believer and his distress from illness; if he knew what is in illness, he would love to be ill until he meets Allah Almighty."
"346","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Abi Humayd narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) raised his gaze to heaven then lowered it. We said: O Messenger of Allah, why did you do this? He said: I marvel at two angels who descended to earth seeking a servant in his place of prayer but did not find him; then they ascended to their Lord and said: O Lord, we used to record for Your believing servant in his day and night such-and-such deeds, but we found You had confined him in Your snare, so we recorded nothing for him. He Almighty said: Record for My servant his deed in his day and night, and do not diminish anything of it; upon Me is the reward of what I confined him from, and for him is the reward of what he used to do."
"347","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Ishaq ibn Yazid al-Hudhali, from Awn ibn Abdullah, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever says in his bowing three times: Glory be to my Lord, the Great, his bowing is complete, and that is its minimum; and whoever says in his prostration three times: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High, his prostration is complete, and that is its minimum."
"348","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Taymi, from Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let not the adhan of Bilal deceive you regarding your sahur, for he only calls the adhan so that your standing one returns and your sleeping one awakes; nor this dawn which is like this - meaning the spreading one - but the dawn which is like this - meaning the elongated one."
"349","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah and Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Uthman, from Ibn Mas'ud - Abu Awanah raised it to the Prophet, while Thabit did not raise it - that he saw a Bedouin wearing a shawl which he had trailed, while he was praying, and he said to him: One who drags his garment out of pride in prayer has nothing with Allah, neither lawful nor unlawful."
"350","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The nations were shown to me at the Hajj season, and I saw my nation filling the plain and the mountain; their multitude and appearance pleased me. It was said to me: Are you pleased? I said: Yes. He said: And with these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning, who do not cauterize, do not take omens, do not seek ruqyah, and rely upon their Lord. Then Ukkashah ibn Mihsan al-Asadi stood and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Allah, make him among them. Then another stood and said: Supplicate to Allah Almighty to make me among them. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ukkashah has preceded you in it."
"351","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: I was a young boy pasturing sheep belonging to Uqbah ibn Abi Mu'ayt at Mecca when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and Abu Bakr came upon me, having fled from the polytheists. He said: O boy, do you have milk to give us to drink? I said: I am entrusted and I will not give you drink. They said: Do you have a young she-goat upon which the male has not yet mounted? I said: Yes, so I brought it to them; Abu Bakr held it, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the udder, supplicated, and the udder filled; Abu Bakr brought him a hollowed stone, and he milked into it, then he and Abu Bakr drank, then they gave me to drink. Then he said to the udder: Contract, and it contracted. Afterwards I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Teach me from this good speech - meaning the Qur'an. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You are a taught boy. So I took seventy surahs from his mouth, which no one disputes with me in."
"352","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, who said: On the day of Badr we were two upon a camel and three upon a camel; the riding companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) were Ali and Abu Lubabah al-Ansari. When their turn to walk came, they said: O Messenger of Allah, ride and we will walk for you. He said: You two are not stronger in walking than I, nor am I less desirous of reward than you."
"353","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, that he used to cut a tooth-stick from arak for the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while the wind would sway him, and there was thinness in his leg; the companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) laughed, and he said: What makes you laugh? They said: At the thinness of his leg. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in Whose Hand is my soul, it is heavier in the balance than Uhud."
"354","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Salamah ibn Kuhayl, from Isa ibn Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Taking omens is polytheism; and there is none of us but Allah removes it through reliance."
"355","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: A man of the people of the bench died, and they found two dinars in his shawl. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Two brands."
"356","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Sulayman al-Shaybani, who said: Zirr ibn Hubaysh passed by us, so I stood to him and asked him about the saying of Allah Almighty: {He indeed saw of the greatest signs of his Lord}. Zirr said: Abdullah said: He saw Gabriel in his form, having six hundred wings."
"357","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Abdullah, who said: I never saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) breaking fast on Friday."
"358","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to fast three days from the beginning of every month."
"359","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, Asim narrated to us, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, how will you recognize those of your nation whom you have not seen on the Day of Resurrection? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Radiant, white-marked, piebald from the traces of ablution."
"360","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim, from Zirr, from Abdullah, who said: I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Whoever lies about me deliberately, let him take his seat in the Fire."
"361","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Qays narrated to us, from Mansur, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar al-Azdi, from Ibn Mas'ud, who said: Some people sat in the mosque - two Qurashis and a Thaqafi, or two Thaqafis and a Qurashi - and one of them said: Do you think Allah hears what we say? One of them said: When we raise our voices He hears, and when we do not raise them He does not hear. The other said: If He hears anything of it, He hears all of it. So I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him, and Allah Almighty revealed: {You were not concealing yourselves lest your hearing should testify against you} the verse."
"362","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from Abu Ma'mar, that an imam of the people of Mecca gave two salutations, so Abdullah said: How did he learn it? Yunus narrated to us, he said: And I was told that other than Abu Dawud said: from Shu'bah, Abdullah said: How did he learn it? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to do it."
"363","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Mansur informed me, who said: I heard Khaythamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrating from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no staying up after prayer except for one of two men: a traveler or one praying."
"364","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Talhah narrated to us, from Zubayd, from Murrah, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: They distracted us from the middle prayer, the afternoon prayer; may Allah fill their houses and graves with fire."
"365","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: I heard Murrah narrating from Abdullah, who said: The truest speech is the Book of Allah, the best guidance is the guidance of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), the worst matters are newly invented ones; what you are promised is coming, you cannot escape it, and only what is not coming is far. Amr said: This phrase (and only what is not coming is far), Murrah narrated to me from Abdullah, or a man from Abdullah."
"366","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Allah Almighty sent down no disease but He sent down a cure for it, except old age; so take to cow's milk, for it grazes from every tree."
"367","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, from Tariq ibn Shihab, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: There is no envy except in two: a man to whom Allah gave wealth and empowered him to spend it in truth, and a man to whom Allah Almighty gave wisdom and knowledge, so he judges by it and teaches it to people."
"368","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from al-Harith ibn Suwayd, from Abdullah, who said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he had a fever; I touched him and said: O Messenger of Allah, you have a severe fever. He said: Yes, I have fever like two men among you. He said: I said: Is that because you have double reward? He said: Yes; by the One in Whose Hand is my soul, no Muslim is afflicted with harm, illness or otherwise, but Allah Almighty removes his sins from him as the tree sheds its leaves."
"369","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Ata ibn al-Sa'ib, from Abu Abd al-Rahman, from Ibn Mas'ud, that he used to seek refuge in prayer from the accursed Satan, from his blowing, spittle, and whispering. Abu Dawud did not raise it to the Prophet, while others raised it."
"370","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: al-Walid ibn al-Ayzar informed me, who said: I asked Abu Amr al-Shaybani, who said: The occupant of this house narrated to us - pointing to the house of Abdullah - who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Which deed is best? He said: Prayer at its time. I said: Then which - or he said: then what? Abu Dawud doubted - He said: Then kindness to parents. I said: Then what - or then which? He said: Striving in the path of Allah. He narrated them to me, and had I asked for more he would have added."
"371","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Asim informed me, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Ibn Mas'ud, who used to say when he gave salutation: O Allah, You are Peace, and from You is peace; blessed are You, O Possessor of majesty and honor. Shu'bah did not raise it to the Prophet, while others raised it."
"372","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from Asim, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to say in some of his supplication: O Allah, as You made my creation good, make my character good. Thus Abu Dawud narrated it; Muhadir said: from Asim, from Awsajah, from Ibn Abi al-Hudhayl, from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"373","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, who said: I heard al-Hudhayl: A man came to Abu Musa and asked him about a man who left his daughter, his son's daughter, and his sister. He said: For the daughter is half, for the sister is half, and go to Abdullah; he will follow me. So he came to Abdullah and mentioned that to him, and he said: I would have gone astray then and would not be of the guided; I shall judge in it with the judgment of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): for the daughter is half, for the son's daughter is a sixth, and for the sister is what remains. So he came to Abu Musa and informed him, and he said: Do not ask us about anything while this learned man is among you."
"374","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Qays, who said: I heard al-Hudhayl, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey; he delayed noon and hastened afternoon, combining them, and delayed sunset and hastened night prayer, combining them. Shu'bah did not say in it: from Abdullah. He said: And it was narrated from Ibn Abi Layla that he connected it from Abdullah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"375","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah and al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Alqamah al-Qari - of Banu Qarah - from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud - he said: And the narration of al-Mas'udi is better - who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on his return from al-Hudaybiyah, and we camped. He said: Who will guard us for our prayer? - Shu'bah said: Who will watch over us? - Bilal said: I will. Al-Mas'udi said in his narration: You will sleep. He said: Who will guard us for our prayer? Ibn Mas'ud said: I said: I will. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will sleep. He said: So I guarded them until, when it was near dawn, what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said overtook me and I slept. We awoke only to the sun. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood and did what he used to do, then said: Had Allah Almighty wished that you not sleep through it, you would not have slept; but He wished it to be for those after you - so it is thus for whoever among you sleeps or forgets. Shu'bah said in his narration: Do thus, whoever among you sleeps or forgets. Al-Mas'udi said in his narration - and it is not in Shu'bah's narration: The mount of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had strayed, so we sought it and found it by a tree with its rein caught on the tree. I said: O Messenger of Allah, hands would never have untied it."
"376","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Sa'q ibn Hazn narrated to us, from Aqil al-Ja'di, from Abu Ishaq, from Suwayd ibn Ghafalah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdullah, do you know which bond of Islam is firmest? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Allegiance for Allah, love for Allah, and hatred for Allah. O Abdullah, do you know which people are most knowledgeable? I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The most knowledgeable of people is the most knowledgeable of them of the truth when people differ, even if he is deficient in knowledge and even if he crawls upon his backside."
"377","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, who said: Shimr ibn Atiyyah al-Asadi informed me, who said: I heard al-Mughirah ibn Sa'd ibn al-Akhram al-Ta'i, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not take landed estates, lest you become desirous of the world. Abdullah said: Baradhan, what is Baradhan; and Medina, what is Medina."
"378","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Shimr ibn Atiyyah al-Asadi narrating from a man of Tayy, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) with the like of it."
"379","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abu Jamrah informed me, from a man of Tayy, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he forbade accumulation - meaning abundance in wealth and children."
"380","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr ibn Mu'awiyah narrated to us, from Abd al-Karim al-Jazari, from Ziyad - not Ibn Abi Maryam - from Abdullah ibn Ma'qil, who said: I was with my father beside him at Abdullah ibn Mas'ud's, and my father said to him: Did you hear the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Remorse is repentance? He said: Yes, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"381","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Hubayrah ibn Yarim, from Abdullah, who said: Whoever comes to a soothsayer and believes him in what he says has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"382","Abu Dawud narrated to us, al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Jami' ibn Shaddad, from al-Aswad ibn Hilal, who said: Abdullah said: Fortune-tellers are the soothsayers of the non-Arabs; whoever believes in a soothsayer has disbelieved in what was revealed to Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"383","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shayban narrated to us, from Mansur, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from al-Bara ibn Najiyah al-Kahili, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The mill of Islam will turn for thirty-five, thirty-six, or thirty-seven years; if they perish, it is the path of those who perished, and if their religion stands for them, it will stand seventy years. Umar said: O Messenger of Allah, with what has passed or what remains? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: With what remains."
"384","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Dharr, from Wa'il ibn Muhanah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), that he said to women: Give charity, for you are most of the people of the Fire. A woman who was not of the eminent women, or of the most sensible of them, said: O Messenger of Allah, in what - or for what, or why? He said: Because you curse often and are ungrateful to the husband."
"385","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, who heard Abdullah ibn Salamah, who heard Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I said: Did you hear it from him? He said: Yes, more than fifty times. He said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was given the keys of the unseen except five: {Indeed Allah, with Him is knowledge of the Hour} to the end of the surah."
"386","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, from Abu Sa'd al-Azdi, from Abu al-Kanud, from Abdullah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade gold rings, or gold circles."
"387","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Maysarah informed me, who said: I heard al-Nazzal ibn Sabrah narrating from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I recited a verse, and a man recited contrary to it, so we came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. Shu'bah said: To the best of my knowledge the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to them: Do not differ, for those before you differed and perished. Shu'bah doubted about: Do not differ; as for the rest it is sound."
"388","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'd ibn Iyad, from Abdullah, who said: The most beloved meat to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was the foreleg, the foreleg of sheep; and poison had been put in it, and he thought the Jews had poisoned him."
"389","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Salamah ibn Kuhayl narrated to us, from his father, from Abu al-Za'ra, from Abdullah, who said: Then Allah Almighty will permit intercession; the Spirit of Holiness, Gabriel, will stand, then Ibrahim, the close friend of Allah, will stand, then Jesus or Moses will stand - Abu al-Za'ra said: I do not know which of them he said - then your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) will stand fourth and intercede; none after him will intercede for more than he intercedes for. That is the praised station which Allah Almighty mentioned: {That your Lord may raise you to a praised station}."
"390","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, who said: Abd al-Malik ibn Umayr narrated to us, from al-Uryan ibn al-Haytham al-Nakha'i, from Qabisah ibn Jabir al-Asadi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursing women who pluck eyebrows, who create gaps between teeth, and who tattoo, those who change the creation of Allah."
"391","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Wabarah, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: Abdullah said: Bathing on Friday is from the practice."
"392","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sulayman ibn al-Mughirah, Mahdi ibn Maymun, and Ibn Fadalah - all of them - narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Qatadah al-Adawi, from Usayr ibn Jabir, who said: We were sitting with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud when a red wind blew, and a man came whose sole refrain was his saying: O Abdullah, the Hour has come; O Abu Abd al-Rahman, the Hour has come. He sat upright, anger visible on his face - he had been reclining on a couch of his - and said: The Hour will not come until no inheritance is divided and no spoils are rejoiced in. Then he said: An enemy of the Muslims will gather against them - and he gestured with his hand. He said: I said to Abu Qatadah: Syria, you mean? He said: Yes. He said: And at that fighting there will be severe apostasy. He said: The Muslims will reinforce one another, meet and fight a fierce battle. He said: Then a contingent will pledge themselves to death and not return except victorious; they meet and fight until night separates them, and both sides return, neither victorious, and the contingent perishes. On the second day another contingent will pledge themselves to death; they meet and fight until night separates them, and both sides return, neither victorious, and the contingent perishes. On the third day another contingent will pledge themselves to death; they meet and fight until night separates them, and both sides return, neither victorious, and the contingent perishes. On the fourth day the remainder of the Muslims will rise against them, and Allah Almighty will grant them victory; the sons of one father, who used to count against a hundred, will look - none of them remains but one man. So what inheritance is to be divided, or what spoils rejoiced in? He said: While they are thus, they will hear of a greater matter: the Antichrist has taken their place among their offspring and families. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Their commander will send a scout, ten horsemen; I know their names, their fathers' names, and the colors of their horses; on that day they are the best horsemen on earth, or among the best horsemen on earth."
"393","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn, from Abd al-A'la, from Kharijah ibn al-Salt, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: It used to be said: Among the signs of the Hour is that mosques are taken as thoroughfares, a man greets a man only from acquaintance, a man and his wife trade together, and the dowries of women and horses become expensive, then become cheap and never become expensive again until the Day of Resurrection. Abu Dawud said: Shu'bah said: We heard nothing from Ibn Mas'ud as it used to be said except this. Al-Thawri narrated this hadith from Husayn, from Abd al-A'la, from al-Salt, who said: I entered the mosque with Abdullah; he bowed, and a man passed by him while he was bowing and greeted him. Abdullah said: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. When he finished he said: It used to be said."
"394","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik, Abu Awanah, and Shayban - all of them - narrated to us, from Abu Ya'fur, from Ibn Abi Aqrab, who said: We came to Ibn Mas'ud and heard him saying: Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth, Allah and His Messenger spoke the truth. We said: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, what is this? He said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Night of Decree is in the middle of the seven; the sun rises without rays. So I watched it, and it was as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had said."
"395","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from one who narrated to him, from Abdullah, who said: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) praying in sandals and leather socks."
"396","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from al-Rukayn ibn al-Rabi', from al-Qasim ibn Hassan, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Harmalah, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) disliked ten things: yellowness - meaning khaluq perfume - wearing gold rings, ruqyah except with the mu'awwidhat, withholding water from its place, displaying adornment outside its proper place, tying amulets, dragging the lower garment, corrupting the child without prohibiting him, dyeing grey hair, and striking with dice."
"397","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Amr ibn Murrah, who said: An elder narrated to me, from an elder of ours whom I did not meet, who said: I entered with Abdullah ibn Mas'ud upon Khabbab, who had been cauterized. Abdullah said: Did you not know we were forbidden this and it was disliked for us? Khabbab said: The affliction was severe, and the physicians said: You have no remedy except that. Abdullah said: I never feared you for this."
"398","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Abu Awanah, Shayban, and Qays narrated to us - all of them - from Jabir, from al-Qasim ibn Abd al-Rahman, from his father, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought captives and would give all the members of one household together, disliking to separate them."
"399","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Qasim, who said: Abdullah sold some slaves of the governorship to al-Ash'ath ibn Qays on credit, then sent to him demanding payment. Al-Ash'ath said: You sold to me for ten thousand, while Abdullah said: I sold to you for twenty thousand. Abdullah said: Choose a man between me and you. Al-Ash'ath said: By Allah, I shall surely choose; you are between me and myself. Abdullah said: By Allah, I shall judge between me and you with a judgment I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): When the two sellers differ and there is no proof between them, it is as the owner of the goods says, or they annul. Hushaym narrates it from al-Qasim, from his father, from Abdullah."
"400","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Imran al-Qattan narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abd Rabbihi, from Abu Iyad, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Beware of belittled deeds, for they gather upon a man until they destroy him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck a parable for them, like people who stopped in a barren land; the people's meal came due, so one man would bring a stick and another a small stick, until they gathered a dark heap of that, then kindled a fire which cooked what was thrown into it."
"401","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Khazim narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abdullah ibn Murrah, from al-Harith al-A'war, from Abdullah, who said: The consumer of usury, its payer, its two witnesses, its scribe, the woman who tattoos and the woman tattooed for beauty, the one who legalizes and the one for whom it is legalized, the withholder of charity, and the one who returns to Bedouin life after emigration - are cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad on the Day of Resurrection."
"402","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from al-Hasan ibn Sa'd, from Abdah al-Nahdi, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty made no sanctity forbidden but He knew that one of you would behold it; indeed I am holding your waists lest you plunge into the Fire as moths plunge."
"403","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abd al-Wahid ibn Wasil narrated to us, from Awf ibn Abi Jamilah al-A'rabi, who said: It reached me from Sulayman ibn Jabir, from Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I am a man who will be taken; so learn the Qur'an and teach it to people, learn the obligations and teach them to people, and learn knowledge and teach it to people, for I shall be taken; knowledge will diminish and trials will appear until two men differ over an obligation and find none to decide between them."
"404","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from al-Hasan, from Imran ibn Husayn, from Abdullah ibn Mas'ud, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) one night until we prolonged the conversation, then we returned to our families; in the morning we came early to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The prophets with their nations and their followers among their nations were displayed to me; a prophet would pass with three of his nation with him, a prophet with a band of his nation, a prophet passing with a few of his nation, a prophet passing with one man of his nation, and a prophet with none of his nation with him, until Musa ibn Imran passed me amid a multitude of the Children of Israel. When I saw them they pleased me, so I said: O Lord, who is this? He said: This is your brother Musa ibn Imran and those of the Children of Israel who followed him. I said: O Lord, where is my nation? He said: Look to your right. I looked, and the hillocks - the hillocks of Mecca - were filled with the faces of men. I said: O Lord, who are these? It was said: These are your nation. It was said: Are you pleased? I said: Yes, I am pleased. It was said: Look to your left. I looked, and the horizon was filled with the faces of men. I said: O Lord, who are these? It was said: These are your nation. It was said: Are you pleased? I said: Yes, my Lord, I am pleased. It was said: With these are seventy thousand who will enter Paradise without reckoning. Then Ukkashah ibn Mihsan, brother of Banu Asad, began and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. He said: O Allah, make him among them. Then another man began and said: O Messenger of Allah, supplicate to Allah to make me among them. He said: Ukkashah ibn Mihsan has preceded you in it. He said: And it was mentioned to us that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May my father and mother be sacrificed for you; if you can be among the seventy, be so; if you are unable and fall short, be among the people of the hillocks; if you are unable and fall short, be among the people of the horizon, for I saw there many people crowding. He said: And it was mentioned to us that some believing men - or people of the believers - discussed among themselves, saying: What do you think these seventy thousand are? Until they concluded of their matters, saying: People born in Islam who continued acting upon it until they died upon it. Their talk reached the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Not as you think; rather they are those who do not cauterize, do not seek ruqyah, do not take omens, and rely upon their Lord. And it was mentioned to us that the Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I hope those of my nation who follow me will be a quarter of the people of Paradise, so we magnified Allah. He said: I hope they will be half. He said: So they magnified Allah. He said: And he recited this verse: {A group of the former ones, and a group of the latter ones}."
"405","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Amr ibn Thabit narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Khumayr ibn Malik, who said: I heard Ibn Mas'ud saying: I am concealing my copy of the Qur'an; whoever can conceal a copy, let him do so, for Allah Almighty said: {Whoever conceals will bring what he concealed on the Day of Resurrection}. I took seventy surahs from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), while Zayd ibn Thabit is but a boy among boys; shall I abandon what I took from the mouth of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)?"
"406","Narrations of Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, may Allah have mercy on him. Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who heard Abu Wa'il, from Hudhayfah, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to a refuse heap of a people and urinated standing, then called for water; I brought him water and he performed ablution and wiped over his leather socks."
"407","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating, who said: It was said to Hudhayfah: Abu Musa is strict concerning urine. Abu Dawud said: Jarir said in this hadith: Abu Musa used to urinate into a bottle and was strict concerning urine. Hudhayfah said: I wish he would not do this; I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he came to a refuse heap of a people and urinated standing."
"408","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, and Hammad ibn Salamah, from Asim - both from Abu Wa'il, who said: Umar said: Who will narrate to us about tribulation? Hudhayfah said: I will. He said: You? He said: O Commander of the Believers, a man's tribulation in his family and wealth is expiated by fasting, charity, enjoining good, and forbidding evil. He said: I do not ask you about this; I ask you about the tribulation before the Hour, surging like the waves of the sea. He said: O Commander of the Believers, between you and it is a closed door. Umar said: Tell me about the door - will it be broken or opened? He said: Rather it will be broken. Umar said: Then it will never be closed until the Day of Resurrection. Abu Wa'il said: We said to Masruq: Ask Hudhayfah about the door, who it is. He asked him, and he said: The door is Umar. People narrated this hadith that Umar said: Who will narrate to us the narration of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning tribulation?"
"409","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Husayn, who said: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Hudhayfah, who said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood for night prayer, he would brush his mouth with the tooth-stick."
"410","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, who said: Hudhayfah said: The hypocrites today are worse than they were in the lifetime of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); then they concealed it, while today they display it."
"411","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hammad ibn Salamah narrated to us, from Asim ibn Bahdalah, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Hudhayfah, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was brought al-Buraq - a white animal above the donkey and below the mule - and he and Gabriel did not leave its back until he brought him to Bayt al-Maqdis; Gabriel ascended with him to heaven, Gabriel sought opening, and showed him Paradise and Hell. Then he said to me: Did he pray in Bayt al-Maqdis? I said: Yes. He said: What is your name, O bald one? I know your face but I do not know your name. He said: I said: I am Zirr ibn Hubaysh. He said: Where do you find he prayed? So I recited the verse: {Glory be to Him who took His servant by night} to the end of the verse. He said: Had he prayed, you would have prayed as you pray in the Sacred Mosque. He said: I said to Hudhayfah: Did he tie the animal to the ring to which the prophets used to tie? He said: Would he fear it would go from him when Allah had brought it to him?"
"412","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Silah ibn Zufar narrating from Hudhayfah, who said: The people of Najran came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: Send to us a trustworthy man. He said: I shall send to you a truly trustworthy man, truly trustworthy, truly trustworthy. The companions of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) aspired to it. He said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Abu Ubaydah ibn al-Jarrah."
"413","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Silah ibn Zufar narrating from Hudhayfah, who said: Islam is eight shares: Islam is a share, prayer is a share, zakat is a share, Hajj is a share, fasting Ramadan is a share, enjoining good is a share, forbidding evil is a share, and striving in the path of Allah is a share; and he who has no share has failed. They mentioned that other than Shu'bah raised it to the Prophet."
"414","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Silah ibn Zufar narrating from Hudhayfah, who said: People will be gathered on one plain and no soul will speak; the first called will be Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who will say: At Your service and Your happiness; good is in Your Hands, and evil is not to You; guided is whom You guided; Your servant before You; I am by You and to You; blessed are You, our Lord, and exalted; glory be to You, Lord of the House. That is His Almighty saying: {That your Lord may raise you to a praised station}."
"415","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from al-A'mash, who said: I heard Sa'd ibn Ubaydah narrating from al-Mustawrid ibn al-Ahnaf, from Silah ibn Zufar al-Absi, from Hudhayfah, that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at night; he would say in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord, the Great, and would say in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High; and he never came upon a verse of mercy but he stopped and asked, and never came upon a verse of torment but he stopped and sought refuge."
"416","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, who heard Abu Hamzah narrating from a man of Abs - Shu'bah thought him Silah ibn Zufar - from Hudhayfah, that he prayed with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - Abu Dawud said: meaning night prayer. When he magnified Allah he said: Allah is Greatest, Possessor of dominion, compulsion, pride, and greatness. He said: Then he recited al-Baqarah. He said: Then he bowed, and his bowing was like his standing, saying in his bowing: Glory be to my Lord, the Great, glory be to my Lord, the Great. Then he raised his head from bowing and stood like his bowing, saying: To my Lord belongs praise. Then he prostrated, his prostration like his standing, saying in his prostration: Glory be to my Lord, the Most High. Then he raised his head from prostration, saying between the two prostrations: My Lord, forgive me, my Lord, forgive me; and he sat as long as his prostration. Hudhayfah said: He prayed four rak'ahs, reciting in them al-Baqarah, Ali Imran, al-Nisa, and al-Ma'idah or al-An'am - Shu'bah doubted."
"417","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, who said: I heard a man at the funeral of Hudhayfah - I think him Rib'i ibn Hirash - who said: I heard the occupant of this bier saying: I have no harm after what I heard from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); if you fight one another I shall enter my house, and if entered upon I shall say: Here, bear my sin and your sin."
"418","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Malik al-Ashja'i, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: We were favored over people with three: our rows were made like the rows of angels, the earth was made for us a mosque and its soil a purifier, and I was given the end of Surah al-Baqarah; they are from a treasure, from a house beneath the Throne."
"419","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Awanah narrated to us, from Abu Malik, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, who said: Your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every good is charity."
"420","Abu Dawud narrated to us, Shu'bah narrated to us, from Hammad, from Rib'i ibn Hirash, from Hudhayfah, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - he said: sometimes he raised it to the Prophet, sometimes he did not raise it - who said: A people will come out of the Fire, stinking, the Fire having scorched them; they will enter Paradise by Allah's mercy and the intercession of intercessors, and will be named the Hell-dwellers."
"421","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatadah, from Abu al-Tufayl, from Hudhayfah, I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: This clan of Mudar will not leave a righteous servant of Allah on earth but it will tempt him and destroy him, until Allah overtakes them afterwards with troops from Him or from heaven, humbling them until it cannot protect the tail of a mountain path."
"422","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Hammam ibn al-Harith, who said: It was said to Hudhayfah concerning a man: This one conveys to the rulers. Hudhayfah said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: No tale-bearer will enter Paradise."
"423","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Yazid Abu Khalid, who heard Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah narrating from Hudhayfah, who said: Whoever sells a house and does not put its price into a house will not be blessed in it. This hadith was narrated from Wahb ibn Jarir, from Shu'bah, raised to the Prophet."
"424","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Qays narrated to us, from Yusuf, from Abu Ubaydah ibn Hudhayfah, from Hudhayfah, raising it likewise."
"425","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: al-Mas'udi and Qays narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Zayd ibn Wahb, who said: Hudhayfah said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) narrated to us two narrations; I have seen one and await the other. He narrated to us: Trustworthiness descended into the roots of men's hearts; they learned from the Qur'an and learned from the practice. Then he narrated to us about its removal, saying: A man sleeps a sleep and a black dot is dotted in his heart; its trace remains in his inside like a blister, like an ember you rolled on your foot and it blistered, and you see it raised with nothing in it. People will wake with no trustworthy one among them. A time came upon me when I did not care whom among you I dealt with: if Muslim, his Islam would return it to me; if Jew or Christian, his agent would return it to me. Now I deal among you with none but so-and-so and so-and-so. A time will come upon people when it is said of a man: How clever, how intelligent, while there is not in his heart the weight of a barley grain of faith."
"426","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Muslim ibn Nadhir narrating from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took the muscle of my leg and said: The due limit of the lower garment is here; if you refuse, then here; if you refuse, the lower garment has no right in the ankles, or: the ankles have no right in the lower garment."
"427","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: I heard Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid saying: We said to Hudhayfah: Inform us of a man close in guidance and manner to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) so we may attach ourselves to him. He said: I know none closer in guidance and manner to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) until his house wall screens him than Ibn Umm Abd. Abd al-Rahman said: Hudhayfah said: The guarded ones among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) knew that Ibn Umm Abd is among the closest of them to Allah in means."
"428","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from al-Walid ibn al-Mughirah, from Hudhayfah, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, I am a man sharp of tongue, mostly against my family. He said: Where are you in seeking forgiveness? I seek forgiveness from my Lord a hundred times a day."
"429","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sharik narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sulaym ibn Abd, from Hudhayfah, who said: The fear prayer is two rak'ahs and four prostrations; if a matter hastens you, fighting and speech have become lawful for you."
"430","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: al-Hakam narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, that Hudhayfah asked for drink; a chief brought him a silver vessel, so he threw it at him and said: I did this only because I had warned him about it; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade drinking in vessels of gold and silver, and wearing brocade and silk, saying: It is for them in this world and for you in the Hereafter."
"431","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abdullah ibn Yasar, from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Do not say: What Allah wills and so-and-so wills; but say: What Allah alone wills."
"432","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Isra'il narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from al-Mughirah ibn Hadhf, from Hudhayfah or Ali, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) shared among the Muslims in their sacrificial animals; the cow is for seven. Other than Abu Dawud says: from Hudhayfah, without doubt."
"433","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, who said: Amr ibn Murrah informed me, who said: I heard Abu al-Bakhtari al-Ta'i narrating from Abu Thawr, who said: I was sitting with Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman and Abu Mas'ud al-Badri when the people of Kufah went out against Sa'id ibn al-As and turned him back - the day of al-Jar'ah. He said: I heard Abu Mas'ud saying: I never thought he would return without blood being shed in it. Hudhayfah said: But by Allah, I knew it would return upon its heels without a cupping-glass of blood being shed in it; I knew nothing of that except something I knew while Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was alive: A man wakes a believer and by evening has nothing of his religion with him, and by evening a believer and by morning has nothing of his religion with him; he fights in the faction of the people - or he said: in the tribulation of the day, Abu Dawud doubted - Allah will kill him tomorrow; his heart is inverted and his backside overcomes him. He said: I said: His lower part? He said: His backside."
"434","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shu'bah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Hudhayfah, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stood among us and informed us of what will be until the Day of Resurrection, except that I did not ask him: What will expel the people of Medina from Medina."
"435","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abu Utbah narrated to us, who said: Umar, freedman of Ghufrah of the people of Medina, narrated to us, from a man of the Ansar of Banu Abd al-Ashhal, from Hudhayfah ibn al-Yaman, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: In the last age there will be a people who say: No decree; if they fall ill do not visit them, if they die do not attend them, for they are the party of the Antichrist, and it is due upon Allah Almighty to join them with him."
"436","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Lahiq ibn Humayd, that a man sat down in the middle of the circle, so Hudhayfa said: Cursed upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the one who sits in the middle of the circle."
"437","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Mijlaz, that a man came to Hudhayfa and said: Did you not see that so-and-so has died? He said: The One who caused him to die is able to cause you to die. Then he sat down in the middle of the circle, so he said to him: Get up, for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) cursed the one who sits in the middle of the circle."
"438","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Subay' ibn Khalid, from Hudhayfa, who said: The Dajjal will emerge, and with him will be a river and a fire. Whoever enters his river, his burden becomes binding and his reward is removed, and whoever enters his fire, his reward becomes binding and his burden is removed."
"439","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Dawud al-Wasiti - and he was trustworthy - narrated to us, saying: I heard Habib ibn Salim, saying: I heard al-Nu'man ibn Bashir ibn Sa'd, saying: We were sitting in the mosque with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and Bashir was a man who withheld his narration. Then Abu Tha'laba came and said: O Bashir ibn Sa'd, do you remember the hadith of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) concerning the rulers? Hudhayfa was sitting with Bashir, so Hudhayfa said: I remember his sermon. Then Abu Tha'laba sat down, and Hudhayfa said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You will remain in prophethood as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it. Then there will be a caliphate upon the path of prophethood, and it will remain as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it. Then there will be a biting kingship, and it will remain as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it. Then there will be tyrannical rule, and it will remain as long as Allah wills it to remain, then He will lift it when He wills to lift it. Then there will be a caliphate upon the path of prophethood. Then he fell silent. He said: Then Umar came, accompanied by Yazid ibn al-Nu'man among his companions, so I wrote to him reminding him of the hadith, and I wrote to him: I hope that the Commander of the Believers will come after the biting kingship and the tyrannical rule. He said: So Yazid took the letter and brought it to Umar, and he was delighted and pleased with it."
"440","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Isma'il ibn Ja'far narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi 'Amr, the freedman of al-Muttalib, from al-Muttalib - thus Abu Dawud said it - from Hudhayfa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The Hour will not come until you kill your leader, and you strike one another with your swords, and the wickedest among you inherit your worldly life."
"441","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Masruq, from Nu'aym ibn Abi Hind, who said: Hudhayfa said: I have seen no reed huts but the reed huts that existed with Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him); they offer no protection against this - meaning Kufa. Abu Dawud said: Al-akhsas are houses we have in Basra made of reeds."
"442","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sharik narrated to us, saying: 'Uthman ibn 'Umayr narrated to us, saying: Zadahn narrated to us, from Hudhayfa, who said: We said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would appoint a successor. He said: If I appointed a successor and you disobeyed him, punishment would descend upon you. Rather, whatever Ibn Mas'ud recites to you, recite it, and whatever Hudhayfa narrates to you, accept it - or he said: listen to it."
"443","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira al-Qaysi narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal al-'Adawi, from Nasr ibn 'Asim al-Laythi, who said: I visited al-Yashkuri, and he said: What has brought you, O Banu Layth? He said: We said: We came to ask you about the hadith of Hudhayfa. He said: Riding beasts had become costly, so we came to Kufa to fetch beasts from it. I said to my companion: I will enter the mosque, and when the market opens I will come out to it. So I entered the mosque, and there was a circle as though their heads had been cut off, gathered around a man. I came and stood, and said: Who is this? He said: Are you from the people of Kufa? I said: No, rather from the people of Basra. He said: Had you been from the people of Kufa you would not have asked about him; this is Hudhayfa ibn al-Yaman. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there evil after this good? He said: O Hudhayfa, learn the Book of Allah and follow what is in it. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there evil after this good? He said: A truce upon smoke. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what is a truce upon smoke? He said: The hearts of a people will not return to what they were upon. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then there will be a blind, deaf tribulation; callers to misguidance - or he said: callers to the Fire. For you to bite onto the root of a tree - meaning a tree - is better for you than following any of them."
"444","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham al-Dastuwai narrated to us, from Qatada, from Subay' ibn Khalid. He said: And Hammad ibn Zayd, Abu 'Ubayd 'Abd al-Warith, and Hammad ibn Najih all narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah Yazid ibn Humayd al-Dubai, from Sakhr ibn Badr, from Subay' ibn Khalid - or Khalid ibn Subay' - who said: Riding beasts had become costly, so we came to Kufa to fetch beasts from it. I entered the mosque, and there was a man of medium build, handsome in his smile, known to be from the men of Hijaz, with people craning toward him. He said: Do not hasten me; I will narrate to you, for we had but recently left ignorance behind, and when Islam came it was a matter the like of which I had never seen. Allah had granted me understanding of the Qur'an. People would ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about good, and I would ask him about evil. I said: O Messenger of Allah, is there evil after this good as there was evil before it? He said: Yes. I said: What is protection, O Messenger of Allah? He said: The sword. I said: Is there anything remaining of the sword, and what comes after it? He said: There will be a truce upon smoke. He said: I said: What comes after the truce? He said: Callers to misguidance. If you see a caliph of Allah on earth that day, cling to him, even if he strikes your back and takes your wealth; and if you see no caliph, then flee until death overtakes you while you are biting onto the root of a tree. I said: O Messenger of Allah, what comes after that? He said: The Dajjal."
"445","Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Habib ibn Abi Thabit, al-A'mash, and 'Abd al-'Aziz ibn Rufay', from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr, give people the glad tidings that whoever says: There is no god but Allah, will enter Paradise."
"446","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Muhajir Abu al-Hasan, who said: We visited Zayd ibn Wahb, and he narrated to us from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was on a journey, accompanied by Bilal. He wanted to call the iqama, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Delay until it cools. Then he wanted to call the iqama and he said: Delay until it cools. Then he wanted to call the iqama and he said: Delay until it cools - three times, meaning for Zuhr - until we saw the shadows of the hillocks. Then he called the iqama and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) prayed. Then he said: The intensity of heat is from the exhalation of Hell, so delay the prayer until it cools."
"447","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Hammad ibn Abi Sulayman, from Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Those who have much are the lowest - or: those who have little - on the Day of Resurrection."
"448","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Yazid ibn Abi Ziyad, saying: I heard Zayd ibn Wahb, from Abu Dharr, who said: A Bedouin came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, the hyenas have devoured us. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I fear for you something other than the hyena more than I fear the hyena for you: when the world is poured upon you abundantly. Oh, would that my nation would not wear gold."
"449","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, having heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: There will be people from my nation whose mark is shaving, who recite the Qur'an without it passing beyond their throats. They will shoot out of the religion - or of Islam - as the arrow shoots through the target. They are the worst of creation and creatures."
"450","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Imran informed me, saying: I heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit narrating from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be rulers who delay the prayer beyond its proper times. So pray the prayer at its time, then go to them; if they have already prayed, you will have secured your prayer, and if not, you will pray with them and it will be voluntary for you."
"451","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Imran narrated to us, having heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit narrating from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When you cook broth, increase its water, then look to a household of your neighbors and give them some of it in kindness."
"452","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Imran informed me, having heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: When Abu Dharr came to 'Uthman from Syria, he said: O Commander of the Believers, do you think I am among a people - by Allah, I am not among them nor will I reach them - who recite the Qur'an without it passing beyond their collarbones, who shoot out of Islam as the arrow shoots through the target, never returning to it until the arrow returns to its notch; their mark is shaving. By Allah, if you commanded me to stand, I would not sit as long as my legs could carry me; and if you bound me with the two wooden loops of a saddle, I would not loosen it until you yourself loosened me."
"453","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran, having heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to hear and obey, even if it be an Abyssinian slave with mutilated limbs."
"454","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal al-'Adawi, saying: I heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit narrating from Abu Dharr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A man's prayer is interrupted, when there is not before him something like the back of a saddle, by a woman, a donkey, and a black dog. He said: I said to Abu Dharr: What is it with the black as distinct from the red? He said: O son of my brother, I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as you asked me, and he said: The black dog is a devil."
"455","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Budayl, from Abu al-'Aliya al-Barra', saying: I heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) struck his thigh and said: How will you be when you remain among a people who delay the prayer? Pray the prayer at its time, then go to them; if you are in the mosque when the iqama is called, pray with them."
"456","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawni, saying: I heard 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a man does a deed for himself and people love him for it? He said: That is the hastened glad tidings of the believer."
"457","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira - and he was among the best of men - narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I was between the Ka'ba and its curtains when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) entered the mosque. He began with the Stone and touched it, then circumambulated the House seven times and prayed two rak'ahs behind the Station."
"458","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he had finished his prayer, and I said: Peace be upon you. He said: And upon you. He said: So I was the first to greet him with the greeting of Islam."
"459","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: How long have you been here? He said: I said: For thirty days and nights. He said: For thirty days and nights! I said: Yes. He said: What was your food? I said: I had neither food nor drink except Zamzam water, and I grew stout until the folds of my belly broke, and I find no trace of hunger in my stomach. He said: Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is blessed; it is a food that nourishes, and a healing for sickness."
"460","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, saying: Humayd ibn Hilal narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: I remained with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as long as I remained. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: A land of palm trees has been shown to me, and I do not see it but Yathrib. Will you convey from me to your people what Allah will benefit them with through you, and reward you among them? I said: Yes. He said: So I set out and met Unays, who said to me: What have you done? I said: I have accepted Islam and believed. He said: I have no aversion to your religion; I have accepted Islam and believed. He said: And we came to our mother and presented Islam to her, and she said: I have no aversion to your religion; then she said: I have accepted Islam and believed. He said: And we came to our people and presented Islam to them, and half of them accepted Islam, while the other half said: When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrives, we will accept Islam. He said: Ima' ibn Rahada al-Ghifari - and he was their chief - used to lead them in prayer. When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) arrived in Medina, the remaining half accepted Islam. And our brothers from Aslam came and said: We accept Islam upon what our brothers from Ghifar accepted Islam upon. Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Ghifar - may Allah forgive it; and Aslam - may Allah grant it peace."
"461","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawni, from al-Munba'ith ibn Tarif, from 'Abdullah ibn al-Samit, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service and your aid, O Messenger of Allah. He said: How will you be when hunger afflicts people, and you come to your bed unable to return to your mosque, and you come to your mosque unable to return to your bed? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Upon you is chastity. He said: How will you be when much death afflicts people, until a grave - meaning the grave - is sold for a servant? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: Upon you is patience. Then he said: How will you be when you see the stones of the oil-press drenched in blood? He said: I said: Allah and His Messenger know best - or: What Allah and His Messenger have chosen for me. He said: Cling to those whom you are from - or: Join those whom you are from."
"462","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr, do you know where the sun goes when it sets? He said: I said: No. He said: It comes to the Throne and prostrates, and it is permitted to return; and it was once said to it: Return from whence you came, so it returns from whence it came. That is its resting place."
"463","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, who said: Whoever builds a mosque for Allah Almighty, even like the nesting place of a sandgrouse, Allah will build for him a house in Paradise. Abu Dawud did not raise it to the Prophet, while Yahya ibn Adam raised it, from Qutba, from al-A'mash."
"464","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Ibrahim al-Taymi, from his father, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, which mosque was placed for people first? He said: The Sacred Mosque, then the Furthest Mosque. He said: I said: And how long between them? He said: Forty years. And wherever the prayer overtakes you, pray, for that is a mosque."
"465","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Qilaba, from Abu Asma' al-Rahabi, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), in what he narrates from his Lord, Blessed and Exalted, who said: I have forbidden wrongdoing for Myself, and I have forbidden it among My servants, so do not wrong one another. Every son of Adam errs by night and day, then seeks My forgiveness, so I forgive him and I do not care."
"466","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Wasil, from al-Ma'rur ibn Suwayd, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Your Lord Almighty said: A good deed is tenfold, and an evil deed is onefold, or I forgive it. Whoever meets Me with wrongdoing filling the earth, without associating anything with Me, I will meet him with forgiveness filling the earth. Whoever intends a good deed but does not do it, a good deed is written for him; whoever intends an evil deed but does not do it, nothing is written against him. Whoever draws near to Me a handspan, I draw near to him a cubit; whoever draws near to Me a cubit, I draw near to him a fathom. Shu'ba did not raise it from Wasil as marfu', while the people raised it from al-A'mash, from al-Ma'rur."
"467","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murra, having heard Suwayd ibn al-Harith, having heard Abu Dharr, saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: It would not delight me to have Uhud as gold with three nights passing over me while I have a dinar - or he said: a weight - of it left with me, except something I set aside for a creditor."
"468","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb narrated to us, from Dawud ibn Abi Hind, from al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Jubayr ibn Nufayr, from Abu Dharr, who said: We fasted Ramadan with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and he did not lead us in prayer for any part of the month, until when it was the night of the twenty-fourth - the seventh of what remained - he prayed with us until nearly a third of the night had gone. When it was the night of the twenty-fifth he did not pray with us. When it was the night of the twenty-sixth - the fifth of what remained - he prayed with us until nearly half the night had gone. I said: O Messenger of Allah, if only you would lead us in voluntary prayer for the rest of our night. He said: No; when a man prays with the imam until he leaves, standing the night is written for him. When it was the night of the twenty-seventh he did not pray with us. When it was the night of the twenty-eighth, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) returned to his family and people gathered for him, and he prayed with us until we nearly missed al-falah. Then - O son of my brother - he did not pray with us for any part of the month. He said: And al-falah is the suhur."
"469","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Mudrik, saying: I heard Abu Zur'a ibn 'Amr ibn Jarir narrating from Kharasha ibn al-Hurr, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: Three whom Allah will not look at on the Day of Resurrection, nor speak to, and for them is a painful punishment. I said: O Messenger of Allah, who are they? They have failed and lost. He said: The one who reminds of his favors, the one who drags his lower garment, and the one who promotes his goods with false oaths."
"470","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Aswad ibn Shayban narrated to us, from Yazid ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, from Mutarrif ibn 'Abdullah ibn al-Shikhkhir, who said: A hadith from Abu Dharr would reach me, and I would long to meet him, so I met him and said: O Abu Dharr, a hadith from you would reach me and I would long to meet you. He said: May Allah bless your father, you have met, so speak. I said: It reached me that you narrate that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) told you that Allah Almighty loves three and hates three. He said: I do not think I would lie about my beloved. I said: Who are the three whom He loves? He said: A man who meets the enemy and fights; and you find that in the Book with you: Indeed Allah loves those who fight in His cause in ranks. I said: And who? He said: A man who has a bad neighbor who harms him, and he bears his harm patiently, so Allah suffices him against him through life or death. He said: And who? He said: A man who was with people on a journey, and they alighted and rested, though drowsiness and sleep had weighed upon them, and they laid their heads and slept, while he stood, performed ablution, and prayed out of awe of Allah and longing for Him. I said: Who are the three whom Allah hates? He said: The miserly one who reminds of favors, and the arrogant boaster - and you find in the Book of Allah: Indeed Allah does not love every arrogant boaster. He said: Who is the third? He said: The merchant - or the seller - who swears much."
"471","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Dinar, from Abu Basra al-Ghifari, from Abu Dharr, who said: Wiping the pebbles is once, and for me not to do it is dearer to me than a hundred black-eyed camels."
"472","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sufyan ibn 'Uyayna narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Najih, from Mujahid, from Abu Dharr, who said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about everything, even wiping the pebbles, and he said: Once. And Sufyan said - from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - likewise."
"473","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murra, having heard Abu al-Bakhtari narrating that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said concerning things for which a man is rewarded, even in coming to his wife. It was said: O Messenger of Allah, how, when it is his desire he fulfills? He said: Do you see, if it were in something unlawful, would he not bear sin? They said: Yes. He said: Likewise he is rewarded. Shu'ba did not raise it as marfu', while al-A'mash said: from 'Amr, from Abu al-Bakhtari, from Abu Dharr."
"474","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Wasil, from Mujahid, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: I have been given five things no prophet before me was given: the earth has been made for me a mosque and a means of purification; I have been aided with awe against my enemy for a month's journey; I have been sent to the red and the black; spoils have been made lawful for me though they were not lawful for any prophet before me; and I have been given intercession, which will reach those of my nation who die without associating anything with Allah. Thus Shu'ba narrated it, while Jarir said: from al-A'mash, from Mujahid, from 'Ubayd ibn 'Umayr, from Abu Dharr, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likewise."
"475","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu al-Husayn, from Ayyub ibn Bashir - or another man - from the judge of the people of Egypt - or a judge, Abu Bishr doubted - that he said to Abu Dharr: Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) use to shake hands with you when you met him? He said: He never met me but he shook my hand. I once came and it was said to me: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sought you, so I came to him, and he met me and embraced me - and that was better and better."
"476","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Ibrahim narrated to us, from Qatada, from 'Abdullah ibn Shaqiq, who said: I said to Abu Dharr: Had I seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), I would have asked him about something. He said: What is it? I said: I would have asked him: Did you see your Lord Almighty? Then Abu Dharr said: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Did you see your Lord? He said: Light - how could I see Him?"
"477","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Yahya ibn Sam, saying: I heard Musa ibn Talha saying: I heard Abu Dharr at al-Rabadha saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr, when you fast three days of the month, fast the thirteenth, fourteenth, and fifteenth."
"478","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu al-Ahwas, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man is in his prayer, mercy faces him, so let him not wipe the pebbles or gravel with his foot."
"479","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Abi Dhi'b narrated to us, from Sa'id al-Maqburi, from his father, from 'Ubaydullah ibn 'Adi ibn al-Khiyar, from Salman al-Khayr, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever bathes on Friday, anoints himself with his oil, perfumes himself with the perfume of his house, then comes to Friday prayer, does not separate two people, prays, and when the imam speaks listens attentively and stays silent, he is forgiven what is between it and the next Friday. Thus Ibn Abi Dhi'b said it - from Salman - while our companions narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from Ibn 'Ajlan, from Sa'id, from his father, from 'Abdullah ibn Wadi'a, from Abu Dharr."
"480","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from Abu 'Umar al-Shami, from 'Ubayd ibn al-Khashkhash, from Abu Dharr, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was in the mosque, and I sat with him. He said: O Abu Dharr. I said: At your service. He said: Have you prayed? I said: No. He said: Stand and pray. So I prayed, then I came to him and sat with him. He said: O Abu Dharr, have you sought refuge with Allah from the evil of the devils of jinn and men? I said: Are there devils among men? He said: Yes, O Abu Dharr. Then he said to me: Shall I not guide you to a treasure from the treasures of Paradise? I said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah, may my father and mother be sacrificed for you. He said: There is no power nor strength except through Allah, for it is a treasure from the treasures of Paradise. I said: And prayer, O Messenger of Allah? He said: An established good; whoever wills may do little, and whoever wills may do much. I said: And fasting, O Messenger of Allah? He said: An obligation that suffices. I said: And charity, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Multiples manifold, and with Allah is more. I said: Which of them is most excellent? He said: The striving of one who has little, and a secret gift to a poor person. I said: O Messenger of Allah, which of what Allah revealed to you is greatest? He said: Allah, there is no god but He, the Living, the Sustainer. I said: Which of the prophets was first, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Adam. I said: Was he a prophet? He said: Yes, a prophet spoken to. I said: How many were the messengers, O Messenger of Allah? He said: Three hundred and fifteen, a great multitude."
"481","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Mundhir al-Thawri, from companions of his, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) left us, and there was not a bird flapping in the sky but he reminded us some knowledge concerning it."
"482","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: al-A'mash informed us, saying: I heard Mundhir al-Thawri narrating from companions of his, from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw two sheep butting each other, and said to me: O Abu Dharr, do you know what they are butting over? I said: No. He said: But your Lord knows, and He will judge between them on the Day of Resurrection."
"483","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Qays narrated to us, from Abu Hashim, from Abu Mijlaz, from Qays ibn 'Abbad, who said: I heard Abu Dharr saying: I swear by Allah, this verse - These are two disputants who disputed concerning their Lord - was revealed only concerning these six men: Hamza, 'Ali, 'Ubayda ibn al-Harith, 'Utba, Shayba, and al-Walid ibn 'Utba."
"484","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from al-Azraq ibn Qays, from a man of Banu Tamim, who said: We were at the door of Mu'awiya, may Allah have mercy on him, and Abu Dharr was with us. He mentioned that he was fasting. When we entered and the tables were laid, Abu Dharr began to eat. He said: So I looked at him, and he said: O red one, what is wrong with you? Do you want to distract me from my food? I said: Did you not tell us you were fasting? - or I said: Did you not claim you were fasting? He said: Yes. Then he said to me: Have you read the Qur'an? I said: Yes. He said: Perhaps you read the single from it but did not read the multiplied: Whoever comes with a good deed shall have ten like it. Then he said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Fasting the month of patience and three days of every month - I think he said: is fasting the lifetime - but this about which there is no doubt: it removes the rancor of the chest. He said: I said: What is the rancor of the chest? He said: The filth of Satan."
"485","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Mahdi ibn Maymun narrated to us, from Wasil, the freedman of Abu 'Uyayna, from Yahya ibn 'Uqayl, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar - and sometimes he mentioned from Abu al-Aswad al-Du'ali - from Abu Dharr, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The deeds of my nation were presented to me, its good and its bad. I saw among the best of their deeds harm removed from the road, and I saw among the worst of their deeds phlegm in the mosque not buried."
"486","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama and Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Abu Qilaba, from a man of Banu 'Amir, who said: I saw Abu Dharr in the mosque of Quba praying, wearing a Qitri cloak. I greeted him but he did not return my greeting. When he finished his prayer he returned it. I said: Are you Abu Dharr? He said: Yes. He said: I found Medina unhealthy, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted me some milch camels and commanded me to drink from their milk and their urine - then Ayyub fell silent at their urine. And I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) among a group of his companions in the shade of the mosque. When he saw me he said: O Abu Dharr. I said: I am ruined, O Messenger of Allah. He said: And what has ruined you? - or he said: And what is that? I said: O Messenger of Allah, I stay away from water and ritual impurity befalls me; shall I pray without ablution - or he said: without purification? So he called for water for me, and an Abyssinian slave girl came with a large cup containing water, shaking, not full. I veiled myself with the camel and bathed. He said: And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu Dharr, pure earth suffices you even if you do not find water for ten years; and when you find water, let it touch your skin. Abu Bishr said: And Abu Hafs narrated to us: Yazid ibn Zuray' narrated to us, from Khalid al-Hadhdha', from Abu Qilaba, from 'Amr ibn Bujdan, who said: I heard Abu Dharr."
"487","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sallam ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Sa'id, from al-Harith ibn Yazid, from Abu Dharr, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, employ me. He said: O Abu Dharr, you are weak, and it is a trust; it will be disgrace and regret on the Day of Resurrection, except for one who takes it by its right and fulfills what is due upon him therein."
"488","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa, that a man said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights so his place may be seen, fights for renown, and fights for spoils; who is in the cause of Allah? He said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the cause of Allah."
"489","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: 'Amr ibn Murra said to me: Abu Wa'il narrated to me a hadith that pleased me. He said: Abu Musa al-Ash'ari narrated to us, that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights to be mentioned, fights so his place may be seen, and fights for such-and-such; who is in the cause of Allah? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is highest is in the cause of Allah."
"490","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa, who said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) leaning upon a staff and said: O Messenger of Allah, a man fights to be mentioned, and fights for such-and-such. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fights so that the word of Allah is supreme is in the cause of Allah Almighty."
"491","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qays and Jarir narrated to us, from Mansur, from Abu Wa'il, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Feed the hungry, free the captive, and visit the sick."
"492","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murra, having heard Abu 'Ubayda narrating from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty extends His hand by night so the evildoer of the day may repent, and by day so the evildoer of the night may repent, until the sun rises from its setting place."
"493","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murra, having heard Abu 'Ubayda narrating from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty does not sleep, nor does it befit Him to sleep. He lowers the balance and raises it; the deeds of the night are raised to Him by day, and the deeds of the day by night. Al-Mas'udi added: His veil is fire; were He to uncover it, the splendors of His face would burn everything His sight reached. Then Abu 'Ubayda recited: Blessed is He who is in the fire and who is around it, and glory be to Allah, Lord of the worlds."
"494","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Murra, from Abu 'Ubayda, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) named himself names for us, among them what we remembered. He said: I am Muhammad, Ahmad, al-Muqaffi, al-Hashir, the Prophet of Repentance, and the Prophet of Battle."
"495","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from Abu Musa, who said: We were with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on a journey. We ascended a valley, and when they descended into it they raised their voices with takbir and tahlil, while the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was upon a mule. He said: O people, be gentle with yourselves, for you are not calling upon one deaf nor absent; you are calling upon One All-Hearing, All-Seeing."
"496","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas ibn Malik, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The example of the believer who recites the Qur'an is like the citron: its fragrance is pleasant and its taste is pleasant. The example of the believer who does not recite the Qur'an is like the date: its taste is pleasant but it has no fragrance. The example of the wicked one who recites the Qur'an is like basil: its fragrance is pleasant but its taste is bitter. The example of the wicked one who does not recite the Qur'an is like the colocynth: its taste is foul and its fragrance is foul."
"497","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda, from his father, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon every Muslim is charity every day. They said: O Messenger of Allah, what if he finds nothing? He said: He works with his hand, benefiting himself and giving charity. They said: What if he does not do so? He said: He helps the one in need, the distressed. They said: What if he cannot? He said: He enjoins good and forbids evil. They said: What if he cannot? He said: Let him withhold from evil, for that is charity for him."
"498","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda, from his father, from Abu Musa al-Ash'ari, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent him and Mu'adh to Yemen, and said to them: Agree with one another, make things easy and do not make them hard, give glad tidings and do not repel."
"499","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda, from his father, from Abu Musa, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, a drink is made among us from honey called bit', and a drink from barley called mizr, and both intoxicate. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"500","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Harish narrated to us, from Talha al-Yami, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Every intoxicant is unlawful."
"501","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammam narrated to us, from Qatada, from Sa'id ibn Abi Burda, from his father, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No believer dies but Allah admits in his place into the Fire a Jew or a Christian. He said: So Abu Burda came to 'Umar ibn 'Abd al-'Aziz, who asked him about the hadith, and he narrated it to him; so he made him swear three times that Abu Musa had indeed narrated it to him from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"502","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ghaylan ibn Jarir, from Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa, from his father, who said: We came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) seeking mounts. He said: By Allah, I will not carry you, and I have nothing with which to carry you. Then some camels were brought and he carried us upon three white-humped ones. When we returned, I said to my companions: By Allah, Allah will not bless us; the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) swore he would not carry us. Go back. We said: O Messenger of Allah, you swore you would not carry us. He said: It was not I who carried you; none carried you but Allah. By Allah - if Allah wills - I do not swear an oath and then see something better than it but I expiate my oath and do what is better."
"503","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hannat narrated to us, from Abu Husayn, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man frees his slave woman then gives her a new dowry, he has two rewards."
"504","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Salih ibn Salih al-Thawri, from al-Sha'bi, who said: Abu Burda narrated to me, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Three will be given their reward twice: a man who had a slave woman, disciplined her and disciplined her well, taught her and taught her well, then freed her and married her; a man of the People of the Book who believed in his prophet, then met the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and believed in him; and a slave who fulfills the right of Allah and the right of his masters. He said: Then al-Sha'bi said to a man with him: Take it without price, for journeys used to be undertaken to Medina for less than this."
"505","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abu Burda ibn 'Abdullah ibn Abi Burda ibn Abi Musa, from his grandfather, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The believer to the believer is like a building, each part strengthening the other."
"506","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: 'Amr ibn Murra narrated to us, having heard Murra narrating from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Many men have attained perfection, but no women have attained perfection except Maryam daughter of 'Imran and Asiya the wife of Pharaoh; and the excellence of 'A'isha over women is like the excellence of tharid over all other food."
"507","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Dawud al-Awdi, from Humayd ibn 'Abd al-Rahman al-Himyari, that Humama - a man among the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - raided Isbahan with al-Ash'ari, and Isbahan was conquered in the time of 'Umar, may Allah be pleased with him. He said: O Allah, Humama claims he loves meeting You. O Allah, if he is truthful, decree for him by his truthfulness; and if he is lying, bring it upon him though he dislikes it. O Allah, do not return Humama from this journey of his. So he died in Isbahan, and al-Ash'ari stood and said: O people, by Allah, in what we heard from your Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - and our knowledge extends no further - Humama is a martyr."
"508","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us: 'Abdullah ibn Nafi' narrated to us, from his father, from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Silk and gold have been made lawful for the females of my nation, and forbidden for its males."
"509","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Mansur, from Ibrahim, from Yazid ibn Aws, that when al-Ash'ari grew heavy with illness, his wife wept over him, and he said: Do you not know what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said? He said: So I asked the woman afterwards: What did he say? She said: He is free of whoever shaves, wails loudly, and tears."
"510","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Abu Sinan, who said: I buried my son Sinan, while Abu Talha al-Khawlani was sitting at the edge of the grave. He said: al-Dahhak ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When Allah Almighty takes the child of a servant, He says to His angels: What did My servant say? They say: He praised You and said: To Allah we belong and to Him we return. He says: Build for him a house, and name it the House of Praise."
"511","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Bishr, saying: I heard Sa'id ibn Jubayr narrating from Abu Musa, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No one of this nation hears of me - neither Jew nor Christian - and then does not believe in me, except he will be among the people of the Fire."
"512","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Zayd narrated to us, from Ayyub, from Nafi', from Sa'id ibn Abi Hind, from Abu Musa, who said: Whoever plays with dice has disobeyed Allah and His Messenger."
"513","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ghalib al-Tammar, saying: Aws ibn Masruq - or Masruq ibn Aws - narrated to us, from Abu Musa, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The fingers are equal. I said: Ten camels for each finger? He said: Yes."
"514","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu Mijlaz, who said: Al-Ash'ari prayed with his companions the 'Isha prayer while between Mecca and Medina, then prayed a rak'a in which he recited a hundred verses of al-Nisa or al-Baqara. It was said to him: What is this? He said: I did my utmost to place my feet where the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) placed his, and to do what he did."
"515","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Tamima, from Abu Musa, who said: Whoever fasts perpetually, Hell is constricted upon him thus - and he formed ninety with a knot of the fingers. Shu'ba did not raise it as marfu', while Sa'id raised it."
"516","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Dahhak ibn Yasar narrated to us, from Abu Tamima, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Whoever fasts perpetually, Hell is constricted upon him thus, and he formed ninety with a knot of the fingers."
"517","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Anas, from Abu Musa, who said: The example of the righteous companion is like the perfume seller: if he does not give you of his perfume, some of its scent reaches you. The example of the evil companion is like the owner of the bellows: if his fire does not strike you, his smoke reaches you. Abu Dawud did not raise it as marfu'."
"518","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, saying: I heard Tariq ibn Shihab narrating from Abu Musa, who said: I came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was halted at al-Batha. He said to me: How did you enter ihram? He said: I said: Labbayk, with an ihram like the ihram of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: You did well; circumambulate the House and between al-Safa and al-Marwa, then exit ihram. So I did, and I visited a woman of Banu Qays who deloused my head. Then I would give people fatwa by it, until a man said to me: O 'Abdullah ibn Qays, gently with some of your fatwa, for you do not know what the Commander of the Believers has introduced concerning the rites after you. He said: I said: Whoever I gave fatwa to about anything, let him wait, for the Commander of the Believers is coming to him, so follow him. He said: So he came, and I went to him and mentioned it to him. He said: If we take by the Book of Allah, then the Book of Allah commands us with completion; and if we take by the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) did not exit ihram until the sacrificial animal reached its place."
"519","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Yunus ibn Jubayr, from Hittan ibn 'Abdullah al-Raqashi, that al-Ash'ari prayed a prayer with his companions. When he sat in his prayer, a man among the people behind him said: The prayer has been affirmed with righteousness and zakat. When al-Ash'ari finished his prayer, he said: Which of you said such-and-such words? The people fell silent. He said: O Hittan, perhaps you said it. I said: I did not say it, though I feared you would rebuke me with it. Al-Ash'ari said: Do you not know what you say in your prayer? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) addressed us and taught us our sunna and explained our prayer to us. He said: Straighten your rows, then let one of you lead you. When the imam says takbir, say takbir; and when he says: Nor of those astray, say: Amin, and Allah will answer you. When he bows, bow, for the imam bows before you and rises before you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So that for that. And when he says: Allah hears whoever praises Him, say: O Allah, our Lord, to You is praise, and Allah will hear you, for Allah Almighty said upon the tongue of His Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): Allah hears whoever praises Him. And when he says takbir and prostrates, say takbir and prostrate, for the imam prostrates before you and rises before you. The Prophet of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: So that for that. When it is at the sitting, let the first of one's words be: Greetings belong to Allah, good things, prayers belong to Allah. Peace be upon you, O Prophet, and the mercy of Allah. Peace be upon us and upon the righteous servants of Allah. I bear witness that there is no god but Allah, and that Muhammad is His servant and Messenger."
"520","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Wuhayb ibn Khalid narrated to us, from Dawud, from Abu Nadra, from Abu Sa'id al-Khudri, that al-Ash'ari sought permission from 'Umar three times but he did not permit him, so he returned. He sent to him: What turned you back? He said: I sought permission three times but was not permitted, and I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: When one seeking permission seeks permission three times and is not permitted, let him return. He said: You shall surely bring me one who knows this, or I shall do to you such-and-such. Abu Sa'id said: Al-Ash'ari came to me trembling, his face turned pale. He stood over a circle of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: I adjure by Allah any man who knows anything of this but to stand forth with it, for I have feared this man for myself. So I said: I am with you. Another said: And I am with you. So he was relieved."
"521","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu al-Tayyah, saying: I heard a black man - who had come with Ibn 'Abbas to Basra - saying: When Ibn 'Abbas came to Basra, he was told hadiths from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). So Ibn 'Abbas wrote to him asking him about them, and al-Ash'ari wrote to him: You are a man of your time, and I narrated nothing of them from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except that I was with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when he wanted to urinate. He inclined toward the soft side of a wall and urinated, and said: The Children of Israel, when urine touched one of them, would cut it off with scissors. Abu Sa'id said: So when one of you wants to urinate, let him seek out a place for his urine."
"522","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr al-Hudhali narrated to us, from Abu Burda ibn Abi Musa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: When you have arrows with you, take hold of their heads lest you wound a Muslim or tear his garment. Al-Ash'ari said: And these people command me to face the pupils of the Muslims with them."
"523","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral being carried quickly in walking. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let tranquility be upon you."
"524","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Za'ida narrated to us, from Layth, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) passed by a funeral being carried quickly, shaking as a waterskin shakes. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Upon you is moderation in walking with your funerals."
"525","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no marriage except with a guardian."
"526","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: 'Imran narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Burda, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he supplicated against a people, would say: O Allah, I place You before their throats, and I seek refuge in You from their evils."
"527","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Awana narrated to us, from Qatada, from Abu Burda, from his father, who said: Would that you had seen us with our Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) when rain had struck us; you would liken our scent to nothing but the scent of sheep."
"528","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, from 'Adi ibn Thabit, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, who said: 'Umar met Asma' bint 'Umays and said: What excellent people you are, were it not that we preceded you to emigration. She mentioned that to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: Rather, you have two emigrations: an emigration to the land of Abyssinia, and an emigration to Medina."
"529","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zuhayr narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burda, who said: A man would say: I have divorced you; I have taken you back. That reached the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), who said: What is with men who play with the bounds of Allah? And Musa ibn Mas'ud said - from Sufyan, from Abu Ishaq, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"530","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Za'ida narrated to us, from Layth ibn Abi Sulaym, from Mujahid, from 'Abdullah ibn Sakhbara, who said: Abu Musa narrated to us, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the funeral of a Muslim man, a Jew, or a Christian passes by you, stand for it; for we do not stand for it, but we stand for those with it among the angels."
"531","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Harith ibn Qudama narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawni, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The gardens of Firdaws are four: two gardens of gold, their ornament, their vessels, and what is in them; and two gardens of silver, their ornament, their vessels, and what is in them. Between them and seeing their Lord Almighty is only the cloak of grandeur upon His face in the Garden of 'Adn. Then it splits with rivers in a hollow in the Garden of 'Adn, then it splits into rivers in Paradise."
"532","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, from Abu 'Imran al-Jawni, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Paradise is beneath the shadows of swords."
"533","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Sulayman ibn al-Mughira narrated to us, from Humayd ibn Hilal, who said: Abu Musa al-Ash'ari said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) accompanied by two men of my people. We reached him while he had a toothstick with which he was cleaning his teeth. They asked him for employment. He said: O Abu Musa, is this what you came for? He said: I said: By Allah, O Messenger of Allah, I did not come for this, nor did they inform me of what was in their minds. He said: So I saw him raise his upper lip with his toothstick, and he said: By Allah, we do not give it to any of you who seeks it. So he sent me and left them. And Yahya ibn Sa'id narrated this hadith from Qurra, from Humayd ibn Hilal, from Abu Burda, from Abu Musa."
"534","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, who said: al-Ash'ari said: I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while I considered Ibn Mas'ud among his household, due to his kindness to them. And Sufyan narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from al-Aswad, from Abu Musa."
"535","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Yahya ibn Kathir and Abu 'Ubayda both narrated to us, from 'Ali ibn Zayd, from Safwan ibn Muhriz al-Mazini, who said: al-Ash'ari addressed us upon the minbar of Basra and said: The wine that was forbidden in Medina was a mixture of unripe dates and ripe dates."
"536","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ziyad ibn 'Ilaqa, from a man, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The passing of my nation is by piercing and plague. They said: O Messenger of Allah, this piercing we know; what is the plague? He said: The piercing of your enemies from among the jinn, and in each is martyrdom. And Abu 'Awana narrates it from Abu Balj, from Abu Bakr ibn Abi Musa, from his father, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"537","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from al-Hasan, from Abu Musa, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: By the One in whose hand is my soul, good and evil are two natures set up for people on the Day of Resurrection. As for good, it promises its people good and congratulates them; as for evil, it says: To me, to me - and they can do nothing but cling to it."
"538","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Dinar narrated to us, from Sa'd ibn Aws, from Misda' Abu Yahya, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught him that it - the sun - sets in a muddy spring."
"539","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, saying: 'Ammar ibn Abi 'Ammar narrated to us, saying: I heard Ibn 'Abbas saying: A time passed over me when I would say: The children of Muslims are with the Muslims, and the children of polytheists are with the polytheists - until so-and-so narrated to me from so-and-so. Then I met the one he had narrated to me from, and he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was asked about them and said: Allah knows best what they would have done."
"540","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Musa ibn 'Abd al-Rahman narrated to me, from Rawh, from Hammad, from 'Ammar, from Ibn 'Abbas, who said: Ubayy narrated to me from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) likewise."
"541","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from Sa'id ibn Jubayr, from Ibn 'Abbas, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, raising it, who said: The boy whom al-Khidr, peace be upon him, killed was fashioned a disbeliever, and love for him was cast upon his parents."
"542","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: 'Asim ibn Bahdala informed me, from Zirr ibn Hubaysh, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah Almighty commanded me to recite the Qur'an to you. He said: So he recited to him: Those who disbelieve. And he recited to him: The abiding practice of the religion with Allah is upright monotheism, not polytheism, nor Judaism, nor Christianity; and whoever does good will not be denied it. And he recited to him: If the son of Adam had a valley he would seek a second to it; and if he were given a second he would seek a third to it. Nothing fills the belly of the son of Adam but dust, and Allah turns to whoever turns."
"543","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn Fadala narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, who said: Ubayy ibn Ka'b said to me: O Zirr, how much do you recite of Surat al-Ahzab? He said: I said: So many verses. He said: It used to rival Surat al-Baqara, and we used to recite in it: The old man and the old woman, when they commit adultery, stone them outright as a deterrent from Allah and His Messenger. Then it was lifted among what was lifted."
"544","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, who said: I asked Ubayy about the two chapters of refuge, and he said: I asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about them, and he said: It was said to me, so I said to you, so say. Ubayy said: So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us, and we say."
"545","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jabir ibn Yazid ibn Rifa'a al-'Ijli narrated to us, saying: Yazid ibn Abi Sulayman narrated to me, saying: I heard Zirr ibn Hubaysh saying: Were it not for fear of your ruler, I would place my hands in my ears, then call out: The Night of Decree is in the last ten, in the seven - three before it and three after it. A report from one who did not lie to me, from a report from one who did not lie to him. Abu Dawud said: Meaning Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"546","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from 'Asim, from Zirr, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that Jibril, peace be upon him, came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) at the stones of al-Mira, and he said to him: O Jibril, I have been sent to an unlettered nation, among them the old woman, the old man, the boy, the girl, and the harsh man who never read a book at all. He said: So Jibril said: The Qur'an was revealed upon seven modes."
"547","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Habib ibn al-Zubayr, saying: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi al-Hudhayl narrating from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, who said: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Khabbab saying: I heard Ubayy ibn Ka'b saying: The Dajjal was mentioned in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) mentioned the Dajjal - and he said: One of his eyes is as though a green glass. And seek refuge with Allah from the punishment of the grave."
"548","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from al-Ajlah, from Dharr, from Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) taught me to recite: So in that let them rejoice."
"549","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Salama ibn Kuhayl and Zubayd al-Iyami, from Dharr, from Ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from his father, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to recite in witr: Glorify the name of your Lord, the Most High; and: Say, O disbelievers; and: Say, He is Allah, One. When he gave salam he would say: Glory be to the King, the Holy - three times, raising his voice with the third. Al-A'mash narrated it from Talha and Zubayd, from Dharr, from Ibn Abza, from his father, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"550","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Kharija ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, saying: Yunus ibn 'Ubayd narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy al-Sa'di, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: For ablution there is a devil called al-Walahan, so beware of him - or he said: so guard against him."
"551","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Ashhab narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: The food of the son of Adam has been struck as an example of the world, even if he salts it and spices it. Sufyan narrated it from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy, from Ubayy, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"552","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Kharija ibn Mus'ab narrated to us, from Yunus, from al-Hasan, from 'Utayy al-Sa'di, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Abu Dawud said: And Ibn Fadala narrated to us, from al-Hasan, raising the hadith as marfu', who said: When death came down upon Adam, peace be upon him, he said: O my sons, I crave some of the fruit of Paradise. So his sons set out seeking it, and they saw the angels, who said: Where are you going, O sons of Adam? They said: Our father craves some of the fruit of Paradise, so we set out seeking that for him. They said: Return, for your father has been ordered to be taken. They came until they reached Adam, peace be upon him. When Hawwa' saw them she recognized them and clung to Adam. He said: Away from me; it is from your side that I was afflicted. Leave me and the angels of my Lord. He said: So they took his soul while they watched, washed him while they watched, shrouded him while they watched, embalmed him while they watched, and prayed over him. Then they turned to them and said: O sons of Adam, this is your practice with your dead, and this is your way."
"553","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ja'far ibn Sulayman narrated to us, saying: Sa'id al-Jurayri narrated to us, from 'Abdullah ibn Rabah al-Ansari, from Ubayy, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to me: O Abu al-Mundhir, which verse in the Book of Allah is greatest? I said: The verse of the Throne. He said to me: May knowledge delight you, O Abu al-Mundhir. By the One in whose hand is my soul, it has a tongue on the Day of Resurrection glorifying Allah at the leg of the Throne. And Sufyan says: from Sa'id, from Abu al-Salil, from 'Abdullah ibn Rabah."
"554","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Thabit Abu Zayd narrated to us, from 'Asim al-Ahwal, from Abu 'Uthman al-Nahdi, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: There was a man of my close kin whose house was the farthest house in Medina. He said: Abu 'Uthman said - while he was narrating among the elders: What is between you and the bridge, or farther. He said: 'Asim said: So I mentioned it to Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: If it was the farthest house in Medina, it is farther than the bridge. Then he said at the end of that: I was only seeking the reward of the footsteps. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: For you is what you sought."
"555","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Salama ibn Kuhayl informed me, saying: I heard Suwayd ibn Ghafala saying: I went out in the morning with Zayd ibn Suhan and Salman ibn Rabi'a, and I found a whip and took it. They said to me: Throw it away. I said: No, but I will announce it; if I find one who recognizes it, well and good, otherwise I will benefit from it. I refused them. When we returned from our expedition it was decreed for me that I performed Hajj. I came to Medina and met Ubayy ibn Ka'b, and I told him of the matter of the whip and their saying. Ubayy ibn Ka'b said: I found a purse containing a hundred dinars in the time of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and mentioned that to him. He said: Announce it for a year. So I announced it, and found none who recognized it, three times. He said: Guard its count, its string, and its container; if its owner comes, well and good, otherwise benefit from it. He said: So I benefited from it. Shu'ba said: Then I met Salama afterwards and he said: I do not know whether three years or one year. This hadith pleased me, so I said to Abu Sadiq: Come and hear it from him."
"556","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Abu Rafi', from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) used to observe i'tikaf in the last ten of Ramadan. He traveled one year and did not observe i'tikaf, so the following year he observed i'tikaf for twenty days."
"557","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu Ishaq narrated to us, saying: I heard 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir narrating from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) led us in prayer and said: Is so-and-so present? They said: No. He said: These two prayers - meaning 'Isha and Fajr - are the heaviest upon the hypocrites. Had they known what is in them, they would have come to them even crawling. The first row is like the row of angels; had you known its excellence you would have rushed to it. A man's prayer with another man is purer than his prayer alone; his prayer with two men is purer than his prayer with one man; and the more, the more beloved to Allah Almighty. And Zuhayr narrated it from Abu Ishaq, from 'Abdullah ibn Abi Basir, from his father, from Ubayy, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"558","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu Jamra informed me, saying: I heard Iyas ibn Qatada, from Qays ibn 'Abbad, who said: I came to Medina to meet the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). None among them was dearer to me to meet than Ubayy ibn Ka'b. I stood in the first row, and 'Umar came out with the companions of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). A man came, looked at the faces of the people, recognized them except me, removed me, and stood in my place. I could not comprehend my prayer. When he prayed he said to me: O young man, may Allah not grieve you, for I did not do what I did out of ignorance; rather the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to us: Be in the row next to me. I looked at the faces of the people and recognized them except you. Then he narrated, and I never saw men stretch their necks toward anything as they stretched toward it. I heard him saying: The people of the knot have perished, by the Lord of the Ka'ba - he said it three times - they have perished and caused perdition. Yet I do not grieve over them, but I grieve over those of the Muslims whom they cause to perish. And the man was Ubayy ibn Ka'b. Abu Dawud said: The people of the knot: what he shed blood over and seized, then claimed."
"559","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim ibn Sa'd narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Bakr ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Marwan ibn al-Hakam, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad ibn 'Abd Yaghuth, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) who said: Indeed, some poetry contains wisdom."
"560","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from Mujahid, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Ubayy ibn Ka'b, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was at the pond of Banu Ghifar when Jibril, peace be upon him, came to him and said: Allah Almighty commands you to teach your nation the Qur'an upon one mode. He said: I ask Allah His pardon and forgiveness, for my nation cannot bear that. Then he came to him a second time and said: Allah Almighty commands you to teach your nation the Qur'an upon two modes. He said: I ask Allah His pardon and forgiveness, and my nation cannot bear that. Then he came to him a third time and said: Allah commands you to teach your nation the Qur'an upon three modes. He said: I ask Allah His pardon and forgiveness, and my nation cannot bear that. Then he came a fourth time and said: Allah commands you to teach your nation the Qur'an upon seven modes; whichever mode they recite upon, they are correct."
"561","Yunus narrated to us, saying: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Abu 'Awn al-Thaqafi informed me, saying: I heard al-Harith ibn 'Amr narrating from the companions of Mu'adh among the people of Hims - he said: and once he said: from Mu'adh - that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he said to him: How will you judge if a case presents itself to you? He said: I will judge by the Book of Allah. He said: And if you do not find it in the Book of Allah? He said: I will judge by the sunna of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). He said: And if you do not find it in the sunna of the Messenger of Allah? He said: I will exert my judgment, sparing no effort. He said: So he struck his hand upon my chest and said: Praise be to Allah who has guided the messenger of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to what pleases the Messenger of Allah."
"562","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-Hakam, from 'Urwa ibn al-Nazzal - or al-Nazzal ibn 'Urwa - from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, inform me of a deed that admits me to Paradise. He said: Splendid, splendid; you have asked about a great matter, yet it is easy for one whom Allah makes it easy for. Pray the prescribed prayer, and give the obligatory zakat. Shall I not inform you of the head of the matter, its pillar, and the peak of its hump? The head of the matter is Islam; whoever submits is safe. Its pillar is prayer, and the peak of its hump is striving in the cause of Allah. Shall I not guide you to the gates of good? Fasting is a shield; charity expiates sin; and a servant's standing in the depth of the night. And he recited: Their sides forsake their beds - to the end of the verse. Shall I not inform you of what controls all that? He said: A rider - or riders - appeared, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) pointed with his hand to his tongue. I said: Will we indeed be taken to account for what we utter with our tongues? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: May your mother be bereaved of you, O Mu'adh; does anything cast people upon their nostrils into the Fire but the harvests of their tongues?"
"563","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Muhammad ibn Rashid narrated to us, from Makhul, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said in this hadith to Mu'adh: As long as you are silent, you are safe; when you speak, it is for you or against you."
"564","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qays ibn Muslim, saying: I heard Abu Ramla narrating from 'Ubaydullah ibn Abi Muslim, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The possessor of three has made it binding. Mu'adh said: So I said: O Messenger of Allah, and the possessor of two? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: And the possessor of two. He said: Meaning one who has sent forth three of his children before him."
"565","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad ibn Salama narrated to us, from Thabit, from Shahr ibn Hawshab, who said: A man narrated to us from Mu'adh, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever sleeps in purity then stirs in the night, he does not ask Allah for anything of the matter of the Hereafter or this world but He gives it to him. Thabit said: The man from whom Shahr narrated to us came to us and narrated to us this hadith."
"566","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: 'Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Yahya ibn Ayyub, from 'Ubaydullah ibn Zahr, from Khalid ibn Abi 'Imran, from Abu 'Ayyash, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: If you wish, I shall inform you of the first thing Allah Almighty says to the believers on the Day of Resurrection, and the first thing they say. They said: Yes, O Messenger of Allah. He said: He says to the believers: Did you love meeting Me? They say: Yes, our Lord. He says: Why? They say: We hoped for Your pardon and Your mercy. He says: I have made My mercy binding for you."
"567","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba and Sallam narrated to us, from Abu Ishaq, from 'Amr ibn Maymun al-Awdi, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said to him: Do you know the right of Allah upon servants? He said: Allah and His Messenger know best. He said: The right of Allah upon servants is that they worship Him and associate nothing with Him; and their right upon Allah Almighty, when they do that, is that He not punish them."
"568","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: al-Mas'udi narrated to us, saying: 'Amr ibn Murra narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Medina and prayed seventeen months toward Bayt al-Maqdis. Then this verse was revealed to him: We see the turning of your face toward the sky - to the end of the verse. He said: So Allah directed him toward the Ka'ba."
"569","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from al-A'mash, saying: I heard Abu Wa'il narrating from Masruq, that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) sent Mu'adh to Yemen, he commanded him to take from every adult a dinar or its value in garments. And others besides Shu'ba said: from Abu Wa'il, from Masruq, from Mu'adh."
"570","Abu Dawud narrated to us: Shu'ba narrated to us, from 'Amr ibn Abi Hakim, from 'Abdullah ibn Burayda, from Yahya ibn Ya'mar, from Abu al-Aswad al-Dili, who said: Mu'adh ibn Jabal was brought a man who had died upon other than Islam, leaving his son a Muslim, so Mu'adh gave him inheritance from him, and said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Islam increases and does not decrease."
"571","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Qurra ibn Khalid narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Zubayr narrated to us, saying: Abu al-Tufayl 'Amir ibn Wathila al-Laythi narrated to us, saying: Mu'adh ibn Jabal narrated to us, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined in an expedition he undertook - and that was in the expedition of Tabuk - between Zuhr and 'Asr, and between Maghrib and 'Isha. He said: I said: What did he intend by that? He said: He intended not to burden his nation."
"572","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Jarir al-Dabbi narrated to us, from 'Abd al-Malik ibn 'Umayr, from 'Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Mu'adh ibn Jabal, who said: Two men reviled one another in the presence of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and one of them became angry until his nose was torn with anger. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I know a word, had he said it his anger would have gone: I seek refuge with Allah from the accursed Satan."
"573","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Ya'la ibn 'Ata', from al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Idris al-'Aidhi, who said: I entered the mosque, wherein were about twenty of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). Among them was a man dark-eyed, bright-toothed; when they differed about anything, he spoke a word and they ended at his word. I asked about him, and he was Mu'adh ibn Jabal. The next day I entered the mosque and he was standing praying toward a pillar. I sat with him, and when I did that he shortened his prayer. I said: By Allah, I love you for the majesty of Allah. He said: By Allah? I said: By Allah. He said: Those who love one another for the majesty of Allah are in the shade of Allah Almighty - I think he said: on the Day of Resurrection - a day when there is no shade but His shade. The prophets, martyrs, and righteous envy them for their nearness to Allah."
"574","Yunus narrated to us: Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, saying: Ya'la ibn 'Ata' narrated to us, from al-Walid ibn 'Abd al-Rahman, from Abu Idris al-'Aidhi, who said: I came to 'Ubada ibn al-Samit, and he said: I shall narrate to you only what I heard upon the tongue of Muhammad (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him): My love is due for those who love one another in Me; My love is due for those who maintain ties in Me; My love is due for those who are sincere to one another in Me - or he said: My love is due for those who spend for one another in Me."
"575","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Zam'a narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Abu Idris al-Khawlani, who said: I was in a gathering of the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), among them 'Ubada ibn al-Samit. They mentioned witr; some said: Obligatory, others said: Sunna. 'Ubada ibn al-Samit said: As for me, I bear witness that I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: Jibril, peace be upon him, came to me from Allah, Blessed and Exalted, and said: O Muhammad, Allah Almighty says: I have made obligatory upon your nation five prayers. Whoever meets them with their ablution, their times, their bowing, and their prostration, he has with Me thereby a covenant that I shall admit him thereby to Paradise. Whoever meets Me having fallen short in anything of that - or a word like it - has no covenant with Me; if I will, I punish him, and if I will, I have mercy on him."
"576","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from 'Ubada ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever loves meeting Allah, Allah loves meeting him; and whoever hates meeting Allah, Allah hates meeting him."
"577","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Shu'ba narrated to us, from Qatada, from Anas, from 'Ubada ibn al-Samit, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The dream of the believer is a part of forty-six parts of prophethood."
"578","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hammad narrated to us, from Thabit and Humayd, from Anas, from 'Ubada ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came out intending to inform his companions of the Night of Decree, when two men quarreled. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I came out intending to inform you of the Night of Decree, but two men quarreled, so it was taken from me. Seek it in the last ten: in the seventh remaining, or the ninth remaining, or the fifth remaining."
"579","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: 'Abd al-Wahid ibn Sulaym narrated to us, from 'Ata' ibn Abi Rabah, who said: al-Walid ibn 'Ubada ibn al-Samit narrated to me, who said: My father called me and said: O my son, fear Allah, and know you will not fear Allah until you believe in Allah and believe in decree, all of it, its good and its evil. If you die upon other than this, you will enter the Fire. I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saying: The first thing Allah created was the Pen. He said: Write. It said: O Lord, what shall I write? He said: Write the decree: what was, and what will be, forever."
"580","Abu Dawud narrated to us, saying: Hisham narrated to us, from Qatada, from Rashid, from 'Ubada ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A woman who dies in childbirth - her child will drag her on the Day of Resurrection by his navel cord to Paradise."
"581","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, who heard Abu Qilabah narrating from Abu al-Ashath, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) took a pledge from us just as he took from the women: that we associate nothing with Allah, steal not, commit not adultery, kill not our children, and disobey him not in what is right. Whoever among you commits any of the forbidden acts carrying a prescribed penalty and it is carried out upon him, it is an expiation for him; and whoever is spared, his affair rests with Allah Almighty - if He wills He punishes him, and if He wills He forgives him."
"582","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Khalid, who heard Abu Qilabah narrating from Abu al-Ashath, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Let none of you slander another. Abu Muhammad said: slander here means talebearing."
"583","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Al-Rabi ibn Subayh narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Sirin narrated to us, from Ibn al-Samit, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Silver for silver, gold for gold, dates for dates, wheat for wheat, barley for barley, and salt for salt, like for like - or he said: weight for weight. Thus Al-Rabi narrated it."
"584","He said: Abu Sufyan and Muhammad ibn al-Mughirah both narrated to us, from al-Numan, from Ibrahim ibn Tahman, from Hisham, from Muhammad, from Abu al-Ashath, who said: A church brought Ubadah and me together, and he said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade - and he mentioned something similar. Salamah ibn Alqamah also reported it from Muhammad ibn Sirin, from Muslim ibn Yasar, from Ubadah."
"585","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, he said: I heard Ibn Musabbih - or Abu Musabbih - narrating from Shurahbil ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah, who said: The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) visited Abdullah ibn Rawahah, who could not move from his bed for him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whom do you count as the martyrs of my nation? They said: Whoever is killed in the path of Allah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Then the martyrs of my nation would indeed be few. Being killed is martyrdom, the plague is martyrdom, abdominal illness is martyrdom, and a woman killed by her child in childbirth is a martyr."
"586","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Harb ibn Shaddad narrated to us, he said: Yahya ibn Abi Kathir narrated to us, he said: Abu Salamah ibn Abd al-Rahman narrated to us, he said: I was informed that Ubadah ibn al-Samit asked the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about the words of Allah Almighty, They shall have glad tidings in the life of this world and in the Hereafter. He said: It is the righteous dream which the Muslim man sees or which is seen for him."
"587","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Jarir ibn Hazim narrated to us, from al-Hasan, from Ubadah. Abu Dawud said: And Ibn Fadalhah mentioned it from al-Hasan, from Hittan ibn Abdullah al-Raqashi, from Ubadah, that when revelation descended upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) its effect was recognized in him. Then the verse, or Allah appoints for them a way, was revealed, and when the revelation lifted, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Take, take; Allah has appointed a way for them. The virgin with the virgin: one hundred lashes and exile for a year; the previously married with the previously married: one hundred lashes and stoning with stones."
"588","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Muslim ibn Abi al-Waddah narrated to us, from al-Ahwas ibn Hakim, from Khalid ibn Madan, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When a man performs the prayer well, completing its bowing and prostration, the prayer says: May Allah preserve you as you have preserved me, and it is raised up. And when he performs the prayer badly, not completing its bowing and prostration, the prayer says: May Allah neglect you as you have neglected me; it is wrapped as a worn garment is wrapped, and his face is struck with it."
"589","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, he said: Abu Bakr ibn Hafs ibn Umar ibn Sad informed me, he said: I heard Abdullah ibn Muhayriz, from men among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - or from a man among the Companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) - who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There will be people from my nation who drink wine, calling it by another name. This hadith was also narrated from Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, from Ibn Muhayriz, from Thabit ibn al-Simt, from Ubadah ibn al-Samit, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"590","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Muhammad ibn Aban narrated to us, from Alqamah ibn Marthad, from al-Shabi, who said: Ubadah ibn al-Samit said in the presence of Muawiyah: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: Whoever suffers a bodily injury amounting to half of the blood-money and pardons, half of his sins are expiated; and if it is a third or a quarter, then in proportion to that. A man said: By Allah, did you hear it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)? Ubadah said: By Allah, I indeed heard it from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"591","Yunus narrated to us, he said: Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Awn ibn Abi Juhayfah, from his father, from al-Bara ibn Azib, from Abu Ayyub, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) went out at sunset and heard a sound, and said: The Jews are being punished in their graves."
"592","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and Hammad narrated to us, from Simak ibn Harb, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Samurah saying: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed as the guest of Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, and whenever he ate food he would send its remainder to him, so Abu Ayyub would look at the place of the hand of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and place his hand there. One day he sent food to him but saw no trace of the fingers of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in it, so he came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said: O Messenger of Allah, I saw no trace of your fingers. He said: There was garlic in it. Shubah said in his narration: Is it forbidden? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: No. And Hammad said in his narration: O Messenger of Allah, you sent me what you did not eat. He said: You are not like me; the angel comes to me, and you are not like me. Thus Abu Dawud informed us. And Ghundar narrated it from Shubah, from Simak, from Jabir, from Abu Ayyub."
"593","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Adi ibn Thabit, from Abdullah ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) combined the sunset and night prayers at Muzdalifah."
"594","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah narrated to us, from Ibn Abi Layla, from his brother, from Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When one of you sneezes let him say: Praise be to Allah in every circumstance; and let the one who responds to him say: May Allah have mercy on you; and let him reply: May Allah guide you and set your affairs right."
"595","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Sufyan ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not lawful for a Muslim to forsake his brother for more than three days; they meet and this one turns away and this one turns away, and the better of the two is the one who begins with the greeting of peace."
"596","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn Budayl al-Khuzai narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid al-Laythi, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, who said: The witr prayer is a right - or an obligation. Whoever wishes may pray witr with seven, whoever wishes with five, whoever wishes with three, and whoever wishes with one; and whoever is overcome should gesture with a gesture. Yazid ibn Harun narrated it from Sufyan ibn Husayn, from al-Zuhri, from Ata ibn Yazid, from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, from the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)."
"597","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Warqa narrated to us, from Sad ibn Said, from Umar ibn Thabit, from Abu Ayyub, that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever fasts Ramadan and then follows it with six days of Shawwal, that is the fasting of the year."
"598","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Abdullah ibn al-Mubarak narrated to us, from Abdullah ibn Uqbah, from Bukayr ibn Abdullah ibn al-Ashajj, from his father, from Ubayd - who is Ibn Tila - from Abu Ayyub al-Ansari, that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade tying up an animal as a target. Abu Ayyub said: Had it been a chicken I would not have tied it up. Abd al-Rahman - who had killed four stout non-Arabs - when he heard this hadith, freed four slaves."
"599","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Quraysh ibn Hayyan narrated to us, from Wasil ibn Sulaym, who said: I came to Abu Ayyub al-Azdi and shook his hand, and he saw my nails long. He said: A man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) asking him, and he said: One of you asks me about news of the heaven while leaving his nails like the claws of birds, in which impurity and dirt gather. Abu Masud reported it from al-Aqadi, from Quraysh, from Sulayman ibn Farrukh, who said: I met Abu Ayyub al-Ansari - and he did not say al-Azdi - and he mentioned something similar."
"600","Abu Dawud narrated to us, he said: Shubah and others narrated to us, from Ubaydah, from Ibrahim, from Sahm ibn Minjab, from Qazaah, from Qarth, from Abu Ayyub, who said: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stayed with me, and he would pray four rakahs before the noon prayer. I asked him about that, and he said: The gates of heaven are opened and are not closed until the noon prayer is prayed. He said: I said: O Messenger of Allah, do you greet between them? He said: No, except at the end of them."
